window.CPLUS_MANUALS = {
  "cp_core": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_core\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"core\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"foundations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"raii\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"intrinsics\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-core-core-foundations-raii-amp-intrinsics\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-core-core-foundations-raii-amp-intrinsics\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_core (Core Foundations, RAII &amp; Intrinsics)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_core</code> module forms the foundational substrate for all <code>C+</code> subsystems. It establishes exact-width scalar types, RAII cleanup macros (<code>Defer</code>, <code>DeferAction</code>), zero-overhead anonymous lambdas (<code>Lambda</code>), C11 <code>_Generic</code> polymorphic printing (<code>Print</code>, <code>Println</code>), hardware bit manipulation intrinsics, and ANSI diagnostic logging.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Exact-Width Types &amp; C11 Polymorphic Print */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> count = <span class=\"tok-number\">42</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-type\">f64</span> ratio = <span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">14159</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Println</span>(count); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Automatically dispatches unsigned long long formatter</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Println</span>(ratio); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Automatically dispatches double formatter</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. RAII Scope Deferral */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">FILE</span> *fp = fopen(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;data.bin&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;rb&quot;</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (fp) {\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Defer</span>(fclose, fp); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Automatically invoked upon block exit</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">// ... work with fp ...</span>\n}\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. Hardware Bit Manipulation */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u32</span> set_bits = <span class=\"tok-func\">BitPopcount32</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">0x00FF00FF</span>); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 16</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> next_p2 = <span class=\"tok-func\">BitNextPow2</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">300</span>);          <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 512</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 4. Diagnostic Logging */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">LogInfo</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Subsystem initialized with %u cores&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-func\">OsNumCpus</span>());</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"ergonomic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"fixed\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"width\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"types\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-ergonomic-fixed-width-types\"><a href=\"#2-1-ergonomic-fixed-width-types\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Ergonomic Fixed-Width Types</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Underlying C Type</th>\n<th>Size</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>u8</code>, <code>u16</code>, <code>u32</code>, <code>u64</code></td>\n<td><code>uint8_t</code>, <code>uint16_t</code>, <code>uint32_t</code>, <code>uint64_t</code></td>\n<td>1, 2, 4, 8 bytes</td>\n<td>Unsigned integers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>i8</code>, <code>i16</code>, <code>i32</code>, <code>i64</code></td>\n<td><code>int8_t</code>, <code>int16_t</code>, <code>int32_t</code>, <code>int64_t</code></td>\n<td>1, 2, 4, 8 bytes</td>\n<td>Signed integers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"usize\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>usize</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"size_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>size_t</code></td>\n<td>4 or 8 bytes</td>\n<td>Memory capacity and array indexing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"isize\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>isize</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"ptrdiff_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ptrdiff_t</code></td>\n<td>4 or 8 bytes</td>\n<td>Signed pointer distance and offsets</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>f32</code>, <code>f64</code></td>\n<td><code>float</code>, <code>double</code></td>\n<td>4, 8 bytes</td>\n<td>IEEE 754 floating point</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>b8</code>, <code>b32</code></td>\n<td><code>uint8_t</code>, <code>uint32_t</code></td>\n<td>1, 4 bytes</td>\n<td>Explicit-width boolean storage</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<span id=\"raii\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cleanup\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"defer\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"deferaction\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-raii-cleanup-defer-amp-deferaction\"><a href=\"#2-2-raii-cleanup-defer-amp-deferaction\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 RAII Cleanup: <code>Defer</code> &amp; <code>DeferAction</code></h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> (*fn)(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_defer_t</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> Defer(func_, arg_) \\\n    __attribute__((cleanup(_cp_defer_cleanup))) <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_defer_t</span> <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_CONCAT</span>(_cp_defer_, __COUNTER__) = { \\\n        .fn = (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> (*)(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *))(func_), \\\n        .arg = (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)(arg_) \\\n    }</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Employs GCC and Clang <code>__attribute__((cleanup))</code> to register a destructor function on the stack.</li>\n<li>Executes predictably in LIFO order upon exiting the enclosing lexical scope (including early returns, breaks, or error paths).</li>\n<li>Allocates zero bytes on the heap.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"anonymous\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"inline\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"lambdas\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"lambda\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-3-anonymous-inline-lambdas-lambda\"><a href=\"#2-3-anonymous-inline-lambdas-lambda\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.3 Anonymous Inline Lambdas: <code>Lambda</code></h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#if</span> defined(__GNUC__) &amp;&amp; !defined(__clang__)\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> CP_HAS_LAMBDA 1\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> Lambda(ret_type, args, body) __extension__ ({ ret_type _cp_lambda args body _cp_lambda; })\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#else</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> CP_HAS_LAMBDA 0\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#endif</span></code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Employs GNU C statement expressions containing a nested function declaration.</li>\n<li>Compiles down to an ordinary function pointer with 0 runtime trampolines and 0 heap allocation.</li>\n<li>In Clang or non-GCC compilers (<code>CP_HAS_LAMBDA == 0</code>), standard static functions or iteration macros (<code>VecEach</code>, <code>VecMap</code>) are used.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"polymorphic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"printing\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"print\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"println\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-4-c11-polymorphic-printing-print-amp-println\"><a href=\"#2-4-c11-polymorphic-printing-print-amp-println\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.4 C11 Polymorphic Printing: <code>Print</code> &amp; <code>Println</code></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Implemented using C11 <code>_Generic</code> compile-time type dispatch.</li>\n<li>Emits formatted strings without runtime type introspection or <code>printf</code> format string vulnerabilities.</li>\n<li>Handles <code>bool</code>, <code>char</code>, signed integers (<code>i8</code>-<code>i64</code>), unsigned integers (<code>u8</code>-<code>u64</code>), floating point (<code>f32</code>, <code>f64</code>), strings (<code>char *</code>, <code>const char *</code>), and pointers (<code>void *</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"hardware\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"bit\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"intrinsics\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-5-hardware-bit-intrinsics\"><a href=\"#2-5-hardware-bit-intrinsics\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.5 Hardware Bit Intrinsics</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Maps directly to target CPU single-cycle instructions via compiler builtins:</li>\n<li><code>BitPopcount</code>: <code>POPCNT</code> instruction on x86-64.</li>\n<li><code>BitClz</code>: <code>LZCNT</code> / <code>BSR</code> (Count Leading Zeros).</li>\n<li><code>BitCtz</code>: <code>TZCNT</code> / <code>BSF</code> (Count Trailing Zeros).</li>\n<li><code>BitBswap</code>: <code>BSWAP</code> (Byte Swap Endianness).</li>\n<li><code>BitRotl</code> / <code>BitRotr</code>: Hardware bitwise rotation instructions.</li>\n<li><code>BitIsPow2</code> / <code>BitNextPow2</code>: Zero-branch bitwise power-of-two arithmetic.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>Implementation</th>\n<th>Runtime Overhead</th>\n<th>Heap Allocations</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Defer</code> / <code>DeferAction</code></td>\n<td>Stack <code>__attribute__((cleanup))</code></td>\n<td>0 cycles until scope exit</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"lambda\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Lambda</code></td>\n<td>GNU Statement Expression</td>\n<td>0 cycles (direct function pointer)</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Print</code> / <code>Println</code></td>\n<td>C11 <code>_Generic</code> compile-time dispatch</td>\n<td>Direct <code>fputs</code> / <code>printf</code> call</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>BitPopcount</code> / <code>Clz</code> / <code>Ctz</code></td>\n<td>Compiler builtin intrinsic</td>\n<td>1 CPU clock cycle</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"bitbswap163264\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>BitBswap16/32/64</code></td>\n<td>Compiler builtin intrinsic</td>\n<td>1 CPU clock cycle</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Defer (1 Arg)</td>\n<td><span id=\"defer\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Defer(func, arg)</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>Execute cleanup function with argument on scope exit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Defer Action</td>\n<td><span id=\"deferaction\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>DeferAction(func)</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>Execute parameterless cleanup function on scope exit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Anonymous Lambda</td>\n<td><span id=\"lambda\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Lambda(ret, args, body)</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>Construct anonymous inline function pointer (GCC)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Print Value</td>\n<td><span id=\"print\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Print(val)</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>C11 type-safe polymorphic print to stdout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Println Value</td>\n<td><span id=\"println\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Println(val)</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>C11 type-safe polymorphic print followed by newline</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assert Message</td>\n<td><span id=\"assertmsg\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AssertMsg(cond, msg)</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>Verify assertion; abort with file/line on failure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Panic</td>\n<td><span id=\"panic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Panic(msg)</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>Print fatal error diagnostic and abort process</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Popcount 32-bit</td>\n<td><span id=\"bitpopcount32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>BitPopcount32(x)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"popcount32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>bit.popcount32(x)</code></td>\n<td>Count set bits in 32-bit word</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Popcount 64-bit</td>\n<td><span id=\"bitpopcount64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>BitPopcount64(x)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"popcount64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>bit.popcount64(x)</code></td>\n<td>Count set bits in 64-bit word</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Count Leading Zeros</td>\n<td><code>BitClz32(x)</code> / <code>64(x)</code></td>\n<td><code>bit.clz32(x)</code> / <code>clz64</code></td>\n<td>Count leading zero bits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Count Trailing Zeros</td>\n<td><code>BitCtz32(x)</code> / <code>64(x)</code></td>\n<td><code>bit.ctz32(x)</code> / <code>ctz64</code></td>\n<td>Count trailing zero bits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Byte Swap</td>\n<td><span id=\"bitbswap163264\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>BitBswap16/32/64(x)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"bswap163264\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>bit.bswap16/32/64</code></td>\n<td>Reverse byte endianness</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rotate Left</td>\n<td><code>BitRotl32(x, s)</code> / <code>64</code></td>\n<td><code>bit.rotl32(x, s)</code> / <code>64</code></td>\n<td>Rotate bits to the left</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rotate Right</td>\n<td><code>BitRotr32(x, s)</code> / <code>64</code></td>\n<td><code>bit.rotr32(x, s)</code> / <code>64</code></td>\n<td>Rotate bits to the right</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Is Power of 2</td>\n<td><span id=\"bitispow2\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>BitIsPow2(x)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"ispow2\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>bit.isPow2(x)</code></td>\n<td>Verify if unsigned integer is power of 2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Next Power of 2</td>\n<td><span id=\"bitnextpow2\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>BitNextPow2(x)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"nextpow2\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>bit.nextPow2(x)</code></td>\n<td>Calculate smallest power of 2 &gt;= x</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Set Log Level</td>\n<td><span id=\"logsetlevel\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>LogSetLevel(lvl)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_log_set_level\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_log_set_level(lvl)</code></td>\n<td>Filter logging threshold</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Log Debug / Info</td>\n<td><code>LogDebug(...)</code> / <code>LogInfo</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>Formatted ANSI colored diagnostic output</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Log Warn / Error</td>\n<td><code>LogWarn(...)</code> / <code>LogError</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>Formatted ANSI colored warning/error output</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Resource Lifetime Safety</strong>: Ensure sockets, file descriptors, arenas, and mutexes are released unconditionally via <code>Defer</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Network Protocol Serialization</strong>: Reorder multi-byte packet header fields into big-endian network order using <code>BitBswap16</code> and <code>BitBswap32</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Capacity Exponential Growth</strong>: Round arbitrary allocation requests up to the nearest power of two using <code>BitNextPow2</code> for cache and ring buffer indexing.</li>\n<li><strong>Fast Bitset Iteration</strong>: Enumerate active flags in bitmasks using <code>BitCtz64</code> and bit-clearing <code>x &amp;= x - 1</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"compilable\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-compilable-example\"><a href=\"#6-complete-compilable-example\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete Compilable Example</h2>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;assert.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">static</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> cleanup_resource(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> *res = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> *)arg;\n    *res = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n}\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> main(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. RAII Deferral */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> active = <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>;\n    {\n        <span class=\"tok-func\">Defer</span>(cleanup_resource, &amp;active);\n        assert(active == <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>);\n    }\n    assert(active == <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Cleanup executed automatically on block exit</span>\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Bit manipulation */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u32</span> mask = <span class=\"tok-number\">0x000F0000</span>;\n    assert(bit.popcount32(mask) == <span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>);\n    assert(bit.clz32(mask) == <span class=\"tok-number\">12</span>);\n    assert(bit.ctz32(mask) == <span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>);\n    assert(bit.isPow2(<span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>) == <span class=\"tok-type\">true</span>);\n    assert(bit.nextPow2(<span class=\"tok-number\">1025</span>) == <span class=\"tok-number\">2048</span>);\n    assert(bit.bswap32(<span class=\"tok-number\">0x12345678</span>) == <span class=\"tok-number\">0x78563412</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. C11 Generic Polymorphic Println */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Println</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--- C+ Core Verification ---&quot;</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Println</span>(<span class=\"tok-type\">true</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Println</span>(1234567890LL);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Println</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">14159</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 4. Logging */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">LogSetLevel</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">CP_LOG_LEVEL_INFO</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">LogInfo</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Core subsystem operational, next pow2 of 45 is %llu&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"tok-type\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">long</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">long</span>)bit.nextPow2(<span class=\"tok-number\">45</span>));\n\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"edge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Edge Cases</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scope Order</strong>: <code>Defer</code> statements in the same lexical block execute in strict LIFO (reverse) order. Ensure dependent resources are deferred after their prerequisites.</li>\n<li><strong><code>BitClz</code> and <code>BitCtz</code> with 0</strong>: Calling <code>BitClz32(0)</code> returns 32 and <code>BitCtz32(0)</code> returns 32 (or 64 for 64-bit variants). Unlike raw compiler builtins which produce undefined behavior for zero on some architectures, <code>C+</code> explicitly guards zero inputs to return the word bit length safely.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_mem": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_mem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"memory\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"subsystem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-mem-memory-subsystem\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-mem-memory-subsystem\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_mem (Memory Subsystem)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_mem</code> subsystem provides high-performance, deterministic memory allocation models designed to eliminate heap fragmentation and allocator lock contention in systems software.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Linear Arena Allocator */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">Arena</span> *arena = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span> * <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> *buffer = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> *)<span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaAlloc</span>(arena, <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span> * <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>));\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaDestroy</span>(arena); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 1 single bulk free</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Scoped Thread-Local Scratch Arena */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span> scratch = <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchBegin</span>();\n<span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *msg = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrFormat</span>(scratch.arena, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Process PID: %d&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-func\">OsPid</span>());\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchEnd</span>(scratch); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Instant rollback in 1 CPU cycle</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"arena\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_arena_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layout-arena-cp-arena-t\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layout-arena-cp-arena-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layout: <code>Arena</code> (<code>cp_arena_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_arena_chunk {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_arena_chunk *prev;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> capacity;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> offset;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> data[];\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arena_chunk_t</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_arena {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> default_chunk_size;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arena_chunk_t</span> *current_chunk;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> total_allocated;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">Arena</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Alignment</strong>: Every bump allocation is aligned by default to <code>CP_DEFAULT_ALIGNMENT</code> (16 bytes on x86-64), ensuring hardware compliance for all scalar types. Arbitrary alignments (e.g. 32-byte AVX or 64-byte cacheline) are supported via <code>ArenaAllocAlign</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Chunk Chaining</strong>: If an allocation exceeds the remaining capacity of <code>current_chunk</code>, a new chunk of size <code>max(default_chunk_size, requested_size)</code> is allocated and chained.</li>\n<li><strong>Bulk Free</strong>: <code>ArenaReset</code> restores the offset of all chunks to 0 without releasing memory to the OS, keeping the virtual address space warm for subsequent frames. <code>ArenaDestroy</code> walks the chunk list and releases all memory back to the system.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"temparena\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_temp_arena_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-struct-layout-temparena-cp-temp-arena-t\"><a href=\"#2-2-struct-layout-temparena-cp-temp-arena-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Struct Layout: <code>TempArena</code> (<code>cp_temp_arena_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">Arena</span> *arena;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arena_chunk_t</span> *chunk;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> offset;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>A lightweight checkpoint (24 bytes) that captures the exact position of an arena's bump cursor. Calling <code>ScratchEnd(temp)</code> restores the pointer in a single CPU register assignment.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"pool\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_pool_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-3-struct-layout-pool-cp-pool-t\"><a href=\"#2-3-struct-layout-pool-cp-pool-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.3 Struct Layout: <code>Pool</code> (<code>cp_pool_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_pool {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> item_size;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> item_count;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *free_list;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> used;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">Pool</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>A fixed-size slab allocator with an embedded intrusive singly linked free-list. Provides true $O(1)$ allocation and arbitrary $O(1)$ deallocation without heap fragmentation.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Arena</th>\n<th>Scratch Pool</th>\n<th>Slab Pool</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Allocation Latency</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ amortized (pointer bump)</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ (1 clock cycle)</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ (free-list pop)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Deallocation Latency</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ bulk</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ rollback</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ free-list push</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Heap Allocations</strong></td>\n<td>0 per object (chunked)</td>\n<td>0 (pre-warmed ring)</td>\n<td>0 during runtime</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Fragmentation</strong></td>\n<td>0% (strictly contiguous)</td>\n<td>0% (strictly contiguous)</td>\n<td>0% (fixed slot size)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Thread-confined</td>\n<td>Isolated per-thread ring</td>\n<td>Requires external lock</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Create Arena</td>\n<td><span id=\"arenacreate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArenaCreate(chunk_size)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"create\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>arena.create(chunk_size)</code></td>\n<td>Instantiate new linear arena</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Allocate</td>\n<td><span id=\"arenaalloc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArenaAlloc(arena, size)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"alloc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>arena.alloc(arena, size)</code></td>\n<td>16-byte aligned bump allocation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Allocate Zeroed</td>\n<td><span id=\"arenaalloczero\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArenaAllocZero(arena, size)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"alloczero\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>arena.allocZero(arena, size)</code></td>\n<td>Zero-initialized bump allocation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Allocate Aligned</td>\n<td><span id=\"arenaallocalign\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArenaAllocAlign(a, sz, align)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"allocalign\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>arena.allocAlign(a, sz, align)</code></td>\n<td>Arbitrary power-of-two aligned alloc</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Reset Arena</td>\n<td><span id=\"arenareset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArenaReset(arena)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"reset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>arena.reset(arena)</code></td>\n<td>Reset cursors without freeing chunks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Destroy Arena</td>\n<td><span id=\"arenadestroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArenaDestroy(arena)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"destroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>arena.destroy(arena)</code></td>\n<td>Release all memory to OS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scratch Begin</td>\n<td><span id=\"scratchbegin\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ScratchBegin()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"begin\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>mem.scratch.begin()</code></td>\n<td>Acquire thread-local checkpoint</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scratch End</td>\n<td><span id=\"scratchend\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ScratchEnd(temp)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"end\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>mem.scratch.end(temp)</code></td>\n<td>Roll back thread-local checkpoint</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create Pool</td>\n<td><span id=\"poolcreate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>PoolCreate(item_sz, count)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"create\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>pool.create(item_sz, count)</code></td>\n<td>Pre-allocate fixed-size slab pool</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pool Alloc</td>\n<td><span id=\"poolalloc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>PoolAlloc(pool)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"alloc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>pool.alloc(pool)</code></td>\n<td>Pop slot from free-list</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pool Free</td>\n<td><span id=\"poolfree\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>PoolFree(pool, ptr)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"free\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>pool.free(pool, ptr)</code></td>\n<td>Return slot to free-list</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Destroy Pool</td>\n<td><span id=\"pooldestroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>PoolDestroy(pool)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"destroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>pool.destroy(pool)</code></td>\n<td>Free slab pool back to OS</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Per-Frame Game / Render Loops</strong>: Allocate all temporary transforms, transient entity buffers, and rendering commands from an <code>Arena</code>, resetting it at the end of each frame (<code>ArenaReset</code>) with 0 kernel syscalls.</li>\n<li><strong>Compiler &amp; AST Parsing</strong>: Allocate abstract syntax tree nodes into an arena during a compilation pass. When compilation completes or errors out, destroy the entire tree in 1 cycle.</li>\n<li><strong>High-Frequency Network Packets</strong>: Pre-allocate a <code>Pool</code> of 4096 network packet descriptors (1500 bytes each) for deterministic $O(1)$ packet reception.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"frame\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"based\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"scratch\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"buffer\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-1-frame-based-scratch-buffer\"><a href=\"#example-1-frame-based-scratch-buffer\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example 1: Frame-Based Scratch Buffer</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> process_sensor_batch(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *raw_data) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span> scratch = <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchBegin</span>();\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> count = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> *readings = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrSplitArena</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">StrFromC</span>(raw_data), <span class=\"tok-string\">&#x27;,&#x27;</span>, scratch.arena, &amp;count);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> sum = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> i = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>; i &lt; count; i++) {\n        sum += (<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span>)atof(readings[i].data);\n    }\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Processed %zu sensors: Average = %.2f\\n&quot;</span>, count, sum / (<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span>)count);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchEnd</span>(scratch); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// All memory reclaimed instantly</span>\n}</code></pre></div>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"simd\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"aligned\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"processing\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-2-simd-aligned-matrix-processing\"><a href=\"#example-2-simd-aligned-matrix-processing\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example 2: SIMD-Aligned Matrix Processing</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> compute_avx_matrix(<span class=\"tok-type\">Arena</span> *arena) {\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 32-byte alignment required for AVX-256 load/store instructions</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *matrix_a = (<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *)<span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaAllocAlign</span>(arena, <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span> * <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span>), <span class=\"tok-number\">32</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *matrix_b = (<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *)<span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaAllocAlign</span>(arena, <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span> * <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span>), <span class=\"tok-number\">32</span>);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Process matrices with zero cacheline unaligned penalty</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>; i &lt; <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>; i++) {\n        matrix_a[i] = (<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span>)i;\n        matrix_b[i] = matrix_a[i] * <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>;\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>No Individual <code>free()</code> in Arena</strong>: An individual object cannot be freed independently of the arena. If you require arbitrary individual element deallocation, use <code>Pool</code> instead.</li>\n<li><strong>Thread Confinement</strong>: An <code>Arena</code> is not thread-safe. Multiple worker threads must not allocate from the same <code>Arena</code> without an external <code>Mutex</code> or <code>ScopedLock</code>. Use <code>ScratchBegin()</code> to obtain isolated per-thread arenas.</li>\n<li><strong>Maximum Chunk Size</strong>: Default chunk size is clamped between 4 KiB and 1 GiB.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_str": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_str\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"strings\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"slices\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"base64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-str-strings-slices-amp-base64\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-str-strings-slices-amp-base64\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_str (Strings, Slices &amp; Base64)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_str</code> module provides zero-allocation immutable string slices (<code>StrView</code>), Arena-backed dynamic string builders (<code>String</code>), and RFC 4648 Base64 encoding/decoding.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Zero-Allocation String Slices */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> full = <span class=\"tok-func\">S</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;  GET /api/v1/telemetry HTTP/1.1  &quot;</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> trimmed = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrTrim</span>(full);\nassert(<span class=\"tok-func\">StrStartsWith</span>(trimmed, <span class=\"tok-func\">S</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;GET&quot;</span>)));\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Arena-Backed String Formatting */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span> scratch = <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchBegin</span>();\n<span class=\"tok-type\">String</span> s = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrFormat</span>(scratch.arena, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Host: %s, Port: %d&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;127.0.0.1&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">8080</span>);\nprintf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;%s\\n&quot;</span>, s.data);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchEnd</span>(scratch);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"strview\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_strview_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layout-strview-cp-strview-t\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layout-strview-cp-strview-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layout: <code>StrView</code> (<code>cp_strview_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_strview {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *data;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> len;\n} <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Borrowing Semantics</strong>: Stores an immutable pointer and byte count. Operations like <code>StrSub</code>, <code>StrTrim</code>, and <code>StrTrimLeft</code> simply increment <code>data</code> and adjust <code>len</code>, never allocating heap memory or copying bytes.</li>\n<li><strong>Literal Macro <code>S()</code></strong>: <code>S(\"literal\")</code> evaluates <code>sizeof(\"literal\") - 1</code> at compile-time, setting <code>len</code> with 0 runtime <code>strlen()</code> calls.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"string\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_string_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-struct-layout-string-cp-string-t\"><a href=\"#2-2-struct-layout-string-cp-string-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Struct Layout: <code>String</code> (<code>cp_string_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_string {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *data;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> len;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> cap;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arena_t</span> *arena;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">String</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>A mutable string builder backed by an <code>Arena</code>. Maintains explicit length while guaranteeing null-termination at <code>data[len] = '\\0'</code> for seamless interop with standard C libc functions.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>StrView</th>\n<th>String Builder</th>\n<th>Base64 Engine</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sub-Slice / Trim</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ zero-allocation</td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Append / Format</strong></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ amortized (on Arena)</td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Encode / Decode</strong></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>$O(N)$ linear time</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Heap Allocations</strong></td>\n<td>0 bytes (borrows memory)</td>\n<td>0 heap calls (Arena-backed)</td>\n<td>0 heap calls (user buffer)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Safe for concurrent reads</td>\n<td>Thread-confined</td>\n<td>Pure reentrant functions</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Literal Slice</td>\n<td><code>S(\"literal\")</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Compile-time StrView constructor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slice from C-Str</td>\n<td><span id=\"strfromc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrFromC(cstr)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"fromc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.fromC(cstr)</code></td>\n<td>Create StrView from null-terminated char*</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Substring</td>\n<td><span id=\"strsub\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrSub(sv, start, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sub\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.sub(sv, start, len)</code></td>\n<td>Slice substring in O(1)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trim Whitespace</td>\n<td><span id=\"strtrim\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrTrim(sv)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"trim\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.trim(sv)</code></td>\n<td>Strip leading and trailing whitespace</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Equals Check</td>\n<td><span id=\"strequals\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrEquals(a, b)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"equals\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.equals(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>Constant-time slice equality check</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Starts With</td>\n<td><span id=\"strstartswith\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrStartsWith(sv, pre)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"startswith\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.startsWith(sv, pre)</code></td>\n<td>Prefix verification</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ends With</td>\n<td><span id=\"strendswith\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrEndsWith(sv, suf)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"endswith\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.endsWith(sv, suf)</code></td>\n<td>Suffix verification</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Find Substring</td>\n<td><span id=\"strfind\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrFind(sv, needle)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"find\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.find(sv, needle)</code></td>\n<td>Search needle, return byte offset (-1 if none)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Split on Arena</td>\n<td><span id=\"strsplitarena\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrSplitArena(sv, d, a, cnt)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"split\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.split(sv, d, a, cnt)</code></td>\n<td>Split into StrView array on Arena</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New String</td>\n<td><span id=\"strnew\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrNew(arena, cap)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"new\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.new(arena, cap)</code></td>\n<td>Create empty mutable string builder</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>String Length</td>\n<td><span id=\"strlen\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrLen(str)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"len\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.len(str)</code></td>\n<td>Current length of String builder</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Append Slice</td>\n<td><span id=\"strappend\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrAppend(str, sv)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"append\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.append(str, sv)</code></td>\n<td>Append StrView to String builder</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Append C-Str</td>\n<td><span id=\"strappendc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrAppendC(str, cstr)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"appendc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.appendC(str, cstr)</code></td>\n<td>Append null-terminated string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Format String</td>\n<td><span id=\"strformat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrFormat(arena, fmt, ...)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"format\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.format(...)</code></td>\n<td>vsnprintf directly into Arena memory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scratch Format</td>\n<td><span id=\"strformatscratch\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StrFormatScratch(fmt, ...)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Temporary format on thread-local scratch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Base64 Encode</td>\n<td><span id=\"base64encode\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Base64Encode(src, len, dst, cap)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"base64encode\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.base64Encode(...)</code></td>\n<td>RFC 4648 Base64 encoder</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Base64 Decode</td>\n<td><span id=\"base64decode\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Base64Decode(src, len, dst, cap)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"base64decode\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>str.base64Decode(...)</code></td>\n<td>RFC 4648 Base64 decoder</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Zero-Copy HTTP/Protocol Parsing</strong>: Tokenize request headers directly into <code>StrView</code> slices without copying header bytes.</li>\n<li><strong>Log Formatting</strong>: Build log lines into a thread-local scratch string using <code>StrFormatScratch</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Serialization</strong>: Encode raw binary telemetry into Base64 for JSON transmission.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"url\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"query\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"string\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"tokenizer\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-url-query-string-tokenizer\"><a href=\"#example-url-query-string-tokenizer\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: URL Query String Tokenizer</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> parse_query_params(<span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> query) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span> scratch = <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchBegin</span>();\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> pair_count = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> *pairs = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrSplitArena</span>(query, <span class=\"tok-string\">&#x27;&amp;&#x27;</span>, scratch.arena, &amp;pair_count);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> i = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>; i &lt; pair_count; i++) {\n        <span class=\"tok-type\">isize</span> eq_pos = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrFindChar</span>(pairs[i], <span class=\"tok-string\">&#x27;=&#x27;</span>);\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (eq_pos &gt; <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>) {\n            <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> key = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrSub</span>(pairs[i], <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span>)eq_pos);\n            <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> val = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrSub</span>(pairs[i], (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span>)eq_pos + <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>, pairs[i].len - (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span>)eq_pos - <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>);\n            printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Param [%.*s] = [%.*s]\\n&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)key.len, key.data, (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)val.len, val.data);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchEnd</span>(scratch);\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Null-Termination of <code>StrView</code></strong>: A <code>StrView</code> slice is <strong>not</strong> guaranteed to be null-terminated (e.g. after <code>StrSub</code> or <code>StrTrim</code>). When passing a <code>StrView</code> to <code>printf</code>, use the <code>%.*s</code> precision specifier (<code>printf(\"%.*s\", (int)sv.len, sv.data)</code>). If you require a null-terminated string, use <code>String</code> or <code>StrFromParts</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Base64 Buffer Sizing</strong>: The destination buffer for <code>Base64Encode</code> must be at least <code>4 * ((src_len + 2) / 3) + 1</code> bytes to hold the encoded output and trailing null byte.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_fs": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_fs\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"high\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"throughput\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"filesystem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"subsystem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-fs-high-throughput-filesystem-subsystem\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-fs-high-throughput-filesystem-subsystem\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_fs (High-Throughput Filesystem Subsystem)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_fs</code> module provides atomic file reads into linear <code>Arena</code> memory, atomic file writes, directory scanning, and path manipulation utilities with zero libc heap fragmentation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">Arena</span> *arena = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span> * <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Atomic Read into Arena Memory */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> content = <span class=\"tok-func\">FileRead</span>(arena, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;/etc/hosts&quot;</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (content.data != <span class=\"tok-type\">NULL</span>) {\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Read %zu bytes from /etc/hosts\\n&quot;</span>, content.len);\n}\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Atomic File Write */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">FileWrite</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;/tmp/config.cfg&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;timeout=30\\n&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">11</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaDestroy</span>(arena);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"atomic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"read\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"engine\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"fileread\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-atomic-read-engine-fileread\"><a href=\"#2-1-atomic-read-engine-fileread\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Atomic Read Engine (<code>FileRead</code>)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Queries file size via POSIX <code>fstat()</code>.</li>\n<li>Allocates a contiguous block of <code>file_size + 1</code> bytes on the specified <code>Arena</code>.</li>\n<li>Reads the entire payload in a single <code>read()</code> system call, appending a trailing <code>\\0</code> null byte.</li>\n<li>Returns a zero-allocation <code>StrView</code> referencing the arena buffer.</li>\n<li><code>FileReadScratch(path)</code> reads the file into the thread-local scratch arena ring, ideal for temporary parsing.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"path\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"sanitization\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"querying\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-path-sanitization-amp-querying\"><a href=\"#2-2-path-sanitization-amp-querying\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Path Sanitization &amp; Querying</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>All path utilities (<code>PathExt</code>, <code>PathBase</code>, <code>PathDir</code>, <code>PathJoin</code>) work with <code>StrView</code> slices to avoid allocating temporary string buffers.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>FileRead</th>\n<th>FileWrite</th>\n<th>Path Operations</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>I/O Complexity</strong></td>\n<td>$O(N)$ file size (single system call)</td>\n<td>$O(N)$ (single write system call)</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ pointer math</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Allocation</strong></td>\n<td>Linear Arena allocation</td>\n<td>0 heap allocations</td>\n<td>0 heap allocations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Null Termination</strong></td>\n<td>Guaranteed (<code>data[len] = '\\0'</code>)</td>\n<td>Preserves binary bytes</td>\n<td>Preserves slice boundaries</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Safe (atomic file descriptor)</td>\n<td>Safe (kernel write synchronization)</td>\n<td>Pure functions</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Read to Arena</td>\n<td><span id=\"fileread\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileRead(arena, path)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"read\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.read(arena, path)</code></td>\n<td>Read file into Arena buffer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read to Scratch</td>\n<td><span id=\"filereadscratch\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileReadScratch(path)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Read file into temporary scratch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Write Buffer</td>\n<td><span id=\"filewrite\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileWrite(path, data, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"write\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.write(path, data, len)</code></td>\n<td>Atomic file write / truncate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Write StrView</td>\n<td><span id=\"filewritestr\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileWriteStr(path, strview)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Write StrView slice directly to disk</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Append Buffer</td>\n<td><span id=\"fileappend\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileAppend(path, data, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"append\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.append(...)</code></td>\n<td>Append bytes to file</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Check Exists</td>\n<td><span id=\"fileexists\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileExists(path)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"exists\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.exists(path)</code></td>\n<td>Check file existence (stat)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Check Is Dir</td>\n<td><span id=\"fileisdir\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileIsDir(path)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"isdir\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.isDir(path)</code></td>\n<td>Check if path is a directory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>File Size</td>\n<td><span id=\"filesize\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileSize(path)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"size\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.size(path)</code></td>\n<td>Query file size in bytes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Delete File</td>\n<td><span id=\"fileremove\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileRemove(path)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"remove\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.remove(path)</code></td>\n<td>Unlink file from filesystem</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create Dir</td>\n<td><span id=\"filemkdir\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileMkdir(path)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"mkdir\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.mkdir(path)</code></td>\n<td>Create single directory (0755)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>List Directory</td>\n<td><span id=\"filelistdir\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>FileListDir(arena, path, &amp;cnt)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"listdir\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>fs.listDir(...)</code></td>\n<td>Read directory entries into StrView array</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Path Extension</td>\n<td><span id=\"pathext\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>PathExt(path_sv)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Extract file extension (e.g. \".log\")</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Path Basename</td>\n<td><span id=\"pathbase\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>PathBase(path_sv)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Extract filename without directory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Path Directory</td>\n<td><span id=\"pathdir\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>PathDir(arena, path_sv)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Extract parent directory path</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Path Join</td>\n<td><span id=\"pathjoin\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>PathJoin(arena, p1, p2)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Join two paths with slash separator</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Config File Ingestion</strong>: Read JSON/YAML/INI configuration files into scratch memory in 1 call.</li>\n<li><strong>Directory Walkers &amp; Asset Loaders</strong>: Iterate asset files in game or web engines using <code>FileListDir</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Atomic State Persistence</strong>: Save telemetry and binary state to disk using <code>FileWrite</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"path\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"inspection\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"file\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"backup\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-path-inspection-amp-file-backup\"><a href=\"#example-path-inspection-amp-file-backup\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: Path Inspection &amp; File Backup</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> backup_config(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *source_path) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span> scratch = <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchBegin</span>();\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> path_sv = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrFromC</span>(source_path);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> filename = <span class=\"tok-func\">PathBase</span>(path_sv);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> backup_dir = <span class=\"tok-func\">S</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;/tmp/backups&quot;</span>);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">FileMkdir</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;/tmp/backups&quot;</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> target_path = <span class=\"tok-func\">PathJoin</span>(scratch.arena, backup_dir, filename);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> data = <span class=\"tok-func\">FileRead</span>(scratch.arena, source_path);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (data.data != <span class=\"tok-type\">NULL</span>) {\n        <span class=\"tok-func\">FileWriteStr</span>(target_path.data, data);\n        printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Backed up %zu bytes to %s\\n&quot;</span>, data.len, target_path.data);\n    }\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchEnd</span>(scratch);\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>File Size Clamping</strong>: Files exceeding available system RAM cannot be mapped into an <code>Arena</code>. For gigabyte-scale datasets, use streaming reads or standard memory-mapped files.</li>\n<li><strong>Symlink Traversal</strong>: <code>FileExists</code> uses <code>stat()</code>, which resolves symbolic links.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_ds": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_ds\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"collections\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"data\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"structures\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-ds-collections-amp-data-structures\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-ds-collections-amp-data-structures\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_ds (Collections &amp; Data Structures)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_ds</code> module provides cacheline-aligned, zero-overhead collections: type-safe stretchy buffer dynamic arrays (<code>Vec(T)</code>), functional inlined iterators (<code>VecEach</code>, <code>VecMap</code>), a lock-free Single-Producer Single-Consumer circular queue (<code>RingBuffer</code>), and Arena-backed singly/doubly linked lists (<code>SList</code>, <code>DList</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Dynamic Type-Safe Vector */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">Vec</span>(<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>) numbers = <span class=\"tok-func\">VecNew</span>(<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">VecPush</span>(numbers, <span class=\"tok-number\">10</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">VecPush</span>(numbers, <span class=\"tok-number\">20</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* In-Place Transformation */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">VecMap</span>(numbers, it, { *it *= <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>; });\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Direct array access */</span>\nprintf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Item 0: %d, Len: %zu\\n&quot;</span>, numbers[<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>], <span class=\"tok-func\">VecLen</span>(numbers));\n<span class=\"tok-func\">VecFree</span>(numbers);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"dynamic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"stretchy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"vector\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"vec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-dynamic-stretchy-vector-vec-t\"><a href=\"#2-1-dynamic-stretchy-vector-vec-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Dynamic Stretchy Vector (<code>Vec(T)</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> len;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> cap;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_vec_header_t</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> cp_vec_header(v) ((cp_vec_header_t *)(v) - 1)\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> Vec(T) T*</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Contiguous Layout</strong>: A <code>Vec(T)</code> is a standard C pointer to <code>T</code>. The hidden header <code>cp_vec_header_t</code> resides directly before element 0 in memory.</li>\n<li><strong>Zero Function Call Overhead</strong>: Indexing (<code>v[i]</code>) compiles directly to machine pointer offsets (e.g. <code>MOV EAX, [RDI + RSI*4]</code>), bypassing all bounds checking or abstraction layers.</li>\n<li><strong>Geometric Growth</strong>: When <code>len == cap</code>, capacity doubles ($2\\times$) using <code>realloc()</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"lock\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"free\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"spsc\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"queue\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"ringbuffer\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-lock-free-spsc-queue-ringbuffer\"><a href=\"#2-2-lock-free-spsc-queue-ringbuffer\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Lock-Free SPSC Queue (<code>RingBuffer</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_ringbuf {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> **buffer;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> capacity;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> mask;\n    _Alignas(<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span>) <span class=\"tok-keyword\">volatile</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> head;\n    _Alignas(<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span>) <span class=\"tok-keyword\">volatile</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> tail;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">RingBuffer</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Cacheline Isolation</strong>: <code>head</code> and <code>tail</code> are aligned to separate 64-byte hardware cachelines (<code>_Alignas(64)</code>), completely eliminating false sharing between producer and consumer CPU cores.</li>\n<li><strong>Bitwise Wraparound</strong>: Capacity is constrained to powers of two, replacing slow integer division with bitwise AND masking (<code>mask = capacity - 1</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Vec(T)</th>\n<th>RingBuffer (SPSC)</th>\n<th>SList / DList</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Element Indexing</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ hardware array access</td>\n<td>N/A (FIFO)</td>\n<td>$O(N)$ traversal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Push / Enqueue</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ amortized</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ lock-free atomic</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ front/back</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pop / Dequeue</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ lock-free atomic</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ front</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Arbitrary Removal</strong></td>\n<td>$O(N)$ shift</td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ for <code>DList</code> with node ptr</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Not thread-safe</td>\n<td>Safe for 1 Producer + 1 Consumer</td>\n<td>Thread-confined</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>New Vector</td>\n<td><span id=\"vecnew\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecNew(T)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"new\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>vec.new(T)</code></td>\n<td>Initialize empty vector pointer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Push Element</td>\n<td><span id=\"vecpush\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecPush(v, val)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"push\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>vec.push(v, val)</code></td>\n<td>Append item, grow capacity (x2)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pop Element</td>\n<td><span id=\"vecpop\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecPop(v)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"pop\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>vec.pop(v)</code></td>\n<td>Decrement length by 1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vector Length</td>\n<td><span id=\"veclen\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecLen(v)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"len\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>vec.len(v)</code></td>\n<td>Get current element count</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vector Capacity</td>\n<td><span id=\"veccap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecCap(v)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"cap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>vec.cap(v)</code></td>\n<td>Get total buffer capacity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Free Vector</td>\n<td><span id=\"vecfree\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecFree(v)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"free\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>vec.free(v)</code></td>\n<td>Deallocate buffer, set v = NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Each Loop</td>\n<td><span id=\"veceach\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecEach(v, idx, val, body)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"each\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>vec.each(...)</code></td>\n<td>Inlined read loop by value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Map Loop</td>\n<td><span id=\"vecmap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecMap(v, it, body)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"map\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>vec.map(...)</code></td>\n<td>Inlined in-place pointer mutation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create RingBuf</td>\n<td><span id=\"ringbufcreate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>RingBufCreate(pow2_cap)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"create\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ringbuf.create(cap)</code></td>\n<td>Allocate lock-free SPSC queue</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>RingBuf Push</td>\n<td><span id=\"ringbufpush\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>RingBufPush(rb, item)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"push\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ringbuf.push(rb, item)</code></td>\n<td>Non-blocking atomic enqueue</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>RingBuf Pop</td>\n<td><span id=\"ringbufpop\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>RingBufPop(rb)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"pop\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ringbuf.pop(rb)</code></td>\n<td>Non-blocking atomic dequeue</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Destroy RingBuf</td>\n<td><span id=\"ringbufdestroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>RingBufDestroy(rb)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"destroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ringbuf.destroy(rb)</code></td>\n<td>Deallocate ring buffer</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Low-Latency Inter-Thread Messaging</strong>: Pass telemetry data or network packets from an I/O thread to an engine thread using <code>RingBuffer</code> without mutex lock contention.</li>\n<li><strong>Dynamic In-Place Array Transformations</strong>: Use <code>VecMap</code> to scale or filter numerical data in contiguous cache memory.</li>\n<li><strong>Graph Adjacency Lists</strong>: Backed by <code>DList</code> allocated on an <code>Arena</code> for zero-leak graph manipulation.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"lock\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"free\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"worker\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"channel\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-1-lock-free-worker-channel\"><a href=\"#example-1-lock-free-worker-channel\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example 1: Lock-Free Worker Channel</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">RingBuffer</span> *channel;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *producer_thread(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg) {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span> i = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>; i &lt; <span class=\"tok-number\">1000</span>; i++) {\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">while</span> (!<span class=\"tok-func\">RingBufPush</span>(channel, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)i)) {\n            <span class=\"tok-func\">ThreadYield</span>(); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Buffer full, yield time-slice</span>\n        }\n    }\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">NULL</span>;\n}\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *consumer_thread(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> received = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">while</span> (received &lt; <span class=\"tok-number\">1000</span>) {\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *data = <span class=\"tok-func\">RingBufPop</span>(channel);\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (data != <span class=\"tok-type\">NULL</span>) {\n            received++;\n        } <span class=\"tok-keyword\">else</span> {\n            <span class=\"tok-func\">ThreadYield</span>();\n        }\n    }\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">NULL</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Vector Reallocation Invalidation</strong>: Calling <code>VecPush</code> may reallocate the vector's memory block. Do not retain direct element pointers (<code>&amp;v[i]</code>) across calls to <code>VecPush</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>RingBuffer Capacity</strong>: <code>RingBufCreate</code> requires capacity to be an exact power of two (e.g. 16, 64, 1024, 4096).</li>\n<li><strong>SPSC Only</strong>: <code>RingBuffer</code> is strictly Single-Producer Single-Consumer. Multiple producers or multiple consumers concurrently writing to the same ring buffer will cause data races. For multi-producer multi-consumer queues, use <code>ThreadPool</code> or <code>Mutex</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_graph": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_graph\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"graph\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"algorithms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"priority\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"queues\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-graph-graph-algorithms-amp-priority-queues\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-graph-graph-algorithms-amp-priority-queues\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_graph (Graph Algorithms &amp; Priority Queues)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_graph</code> module provides adjacency-list graph representations backed entirely by linear <code>Arena</code> memory, supporting Breadth-First Search (BFS), Depth-First Search (DFS), and Dijkstra's Shortest Path algorithm with a 4-ary min-heap priority queue.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">Arena</span> *arena = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span> * <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-type\">Graph</span> g = <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphNew</span>(arena, <span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"tok-type\">false</span>); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 4 nodes, undirected</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">GraphAddEdge</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">GraphAddEdge</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">5</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">GraphAddEdge</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">f64</span> dist[<span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>];\n<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> prev[<span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>];\n<span class=\"tok-func\">GraphDijkstra</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, dist, prev);\n\nprintf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Shortest path from 0 to 3: %.2f\\n&quot;</span>, dist[<span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>]); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 6.50</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaDestroy</span>(arena); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 0 memory leaks</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"graph\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_graph_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"and\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"graphedge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_graph_edge_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layout-graph-cp-graph-t-and-graphedge-cp-graph-edge-t\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layout-graph-cp-graph-t-and-graphedge-cp-graph-edge-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layout: <code>Graph</code> (<code>cp_graph_t</code>) and <code>GraphEdge</code> (<code>cp_graph_edge_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_graph_edge {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> to;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">f64</span> weight;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_graph_edge *next;\n} <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphEdge</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_graph {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> node_count;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> edge_count;\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphEdge</span> **adj;\n    b32 is_directed;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arena_t</span> *arena;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">Graph</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Zero Heap Fragmentation</strong>: The adjacency list node heads (<code>adj</code>) and all <code>GraphEdge</code> link nodes are allocated contiguously from an <code>Arena</code>. Building a 100,000-edge graph issues 0 individual <code>malloc()</code> calls.</li>\n<li><strong>4-ary Min-Heap Dijkstra</strong>: <code>GraphDijkstra</code> utilizes a 4-ary min-heap priority queue. 4-ary heaps feature shallower tree depths than standard binary heaps, increasing L1 cacheline hit rates during heap sift-up and sift-down operations.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Guarantee</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Add Edge</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$</td>\n<td>Prepends edge node to adjacency list</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>BFS / DFS</strong></td>\n<td>$O(V + E)$</td>\n<td>Linear traversal of reachable vertices</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Dijkstra Shortest Path</strong></td>\n<td>$O((V + E) \\log V)$</td>\n<td>Accelerated via 4-ary min-heap</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Allocation</strong></td>\n<td>Linear Arena allocation</td>\n<td>Reclaimed entirely via <code>ArenaDestroy</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Thread-confined</td>\n<td>Safe for concurrent reads if not mutated</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>New Graph</td>\n<td><span id=\"graphnew\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>GraphNew(arena, nodes, directed)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"create\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>graph.create(...)</code></td>\n<td>Initialize graph with node count</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Add Edge</td>\n<td><span id=\"graphaddedge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>GraphAddEdge(g, from, to, weight)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"addedge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>graph.addEdge(...)</code></td>\n<td>Insert weighted edge (undirected inserts both)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Node Count</td>\n<td><span id=\"graphnodecount\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>GraphNodeCount(g)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"nodecount\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>graph.nodeCount(g)</code></td>\n<td>Query total number of vertices</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Edge Count</td>\n<td><span id=\"graphedgecount\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>GraphEdgeCount(g)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"edgecount\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>graph.edgeCount(g)</code></td>\n<td>Query total number of edges</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>BFS Traversal</td>\n<td><span id=\"graphbfs\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>GraphBfs(g, start, visitor, data)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"bfs\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>graph.bfs(...)</code></td>\n<td>Breadth-First Search</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DFS Traversal</td>\n<td><span id=\"graphdfs\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>GraphDfs(g, start, visitor, data)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"dfs\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>graph.dfs(...)</code></td>\n<td>Depth-First Search</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dijkstra</td>\n<td><span id=\"graphdijkstra\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>GraphDijkstra(g, start, dist, prev)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"dijkstra\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>graph.dijkstra(...)</code></td>\n<td>Single-source shortest path</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Network Topology &amp; Routing</strong>: Compute lowest-latency paths between network nodes using <code>GraphDijkstra</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Dependency Resolution</strong>: Topological sorting and reachability checks for build systems and package managers.</li>\n<li><strong>Game Navigation Meshes (NavMesh)</strong>: Fast pathfinding across polygonal navigation graph waypoints.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"bfs\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"visitor\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-bfs-visitor\"><a href=\"#example-bfs-visitor\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: BFS Visitor</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> print_node(<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> node, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *user_data) {\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Visited node %zu\\n&quot;</span>, node);\n}\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> traverse_network(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span> scratch = <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchBegin</span>();\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">Graph</span> g = <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphNew</span>(scratch.arena, <span class=\"tok-number\">5</span>, <span class=\"tok-type\">true</span>);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphAddEdge</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphAddEdge</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphAddEdge</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphAddEdge</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    \n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--- BFS Traversal ---\\n&quot;</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">GraphBfs</span>(&amp;g, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, print_node, <span class=\"tok-type\">NULL</span>);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchEnd</span>(scratch);\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fixed Node Count</strong>: <code>GraphNew</code> fixes the maximum number of nodes at initialization. Node IDs are 0-indexed integers from <code>0</code> to <code>node_count - 1</code>. If your vertices have string names, map them to integers using <code>HashMap</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Non-Negative Weights</strong>: <code>GraphDijkstra</code> requires non-negative edge weights ($w \\ge 0$). Graphs with negative edges require Bellman-Ford (not included).</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_algo": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_algo\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"algorithms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"fast\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"prng\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-algo-algorithms-amp-fast-prng\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-algo-algorithms-amp-fast-prng\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_algo (Algorithms &amp; Fast PRNG)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_algo</code> module provides high-performance IntroSort ($O(N \\log N)$ worst-case), linear $O(N)$ RadixSort for 32-bit unsigned integers, binary search, array permutation utilities, and the lock-free Xoshiro256** pseudo-random generator.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Fast Linear O(N) Radix Sort */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u32</span> keys[] = { <span class=\"tok-number\">9821</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">102</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">54</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">88123</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">712</span> };\n<span class=\"tok-func\">AlgoRadixSortU32</span>(keys, <span class=\"tok-number\">6</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Binary Search in Sorted Array */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">isize</span> idx = <span class=\"tok-func\">AlgoBinarySearchU32</span>(keys, <span class=\"tok-number\">6</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">102</span>);\nassert(idx != -<span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. Sub-Nanosecond PRNG (Xoshiro256**) */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Rng</span> rng;\n<span class=\"tok-func\">RandInit</span>(&amp;rng, 123456789ULL);\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> random_val = <span class=\"tok-func\">RandU64</span>(&amp;rng);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"introsort\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"hybrid\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"algosort\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-introsort-hybrid-architecture-algosort\"><a href=\"#2-1-introsort-hybrid-architecture-algosort\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 IntroSort Hybrid Architecture (<code>AlgoSort</code>)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Combines three sorting techniques:</li>\n<li><strong>QuickSort</strong>: Used for initial partitioning with median-of-three pivot selection.</li>\n<li><strong>HeapSort Fallback</strong>: If recursion depth exceeds $2 \\times \\lfloor\\log_2 N\\rfloor$, IntroSort switches to HeapSort to prevent worst-case $O(N^2)$ quadratic degradation.</li>\n<li><strong>InsertionSort</strong>: Partitions smaller than 16 elements switch to inlined InsertionSort for optimal instruction pipeline utilization.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"linear\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"radixsort\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"algoradixsortu32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-linear-radixsort-algoradixsortu32\"><a href=\"#2-2-linear-radixsort-algoradixsortu32\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Linear RadixSort (<code>AlgoRadixSortU32</code>)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Least-Significant-Digit (LSD) Radix Sort processing 8 bits per pass (4 passes total for 32-bit words).</li>\n<li>Uses 256 counting histogram buckets per pass, sorting arrays in strictly linear $O(N)$ time.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"xoshiro256\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"prng\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"rng\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_rand_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-3-xoshiro256-prng-rng-cp-rand-t\"><a href=\"#2-3-xoshiro256-prng-rng-cp-rand-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.3 Xoshiro256** PRNG (<code>Rng</code> / <code>cp_rand_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> s[<span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>];\n} <span class=\"tok-func\">Rng</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Passes all standard BigCrush statistical tests. Generates 64-bit random values in ~0.8 nanoseconds with 0 locks.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>IntroSort</th>\n<th>RadixSort U32</th>\n<th>Binary Search</th>\n<th>Xoshiro256**</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Time Complexity</strong></td>\n<td>$O(N \\log N)$ guaranteed</td>\n<td>$O(N)$ strictly linear</td>\n<td>$O(\\log N)$</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ (&lt; 1 ns/op)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Auxiliary Memory</strong></td>\n<td>$O(\\log N)$ stack frames</td>\n<td>1 scratch buffer</td>\n<td>$O(1)$</td>\n<td>32 bytes on stack</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Stability</strong></td>\n<td>Unstable</td>\n<td>Stable</td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Deterministic</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Reentrant</td>\n<td>Reentrant</td>\n<td>Pure function</td>\n<td>Isolated per state</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Generic Sort</td>\n<td><span id=\"algosort\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoSort(base, n, sz, cmp)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sort\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.sort(...)</code></td>\n<td>IntroSort hybrid sorter</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sort i32</td>\n<td><span id=\"algosorti32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoSortI32(arr, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sorti32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.sortI32(arr, len)</code></td>\n<td>Inlined integer sort</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sort u32</td>\n<td><span id=\"algosortu32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoSortU32(arr, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sortu32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.sortU32(arr, len)</code></td>\n<td>Inlined unsigned integer sort</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sort f32</td>\n<td><span id=\"algosortf32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoSortF32(arr, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sortf32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.sortF32(arr, len)</code></td>\n<td>Inlined float sort</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Radix Sort</td>\n<td><span id=\"algoradixsortu32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoRadixSortU32(arr, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"radixsortu32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.radixSortU32(...)</code></td>\n<td>O(N) linear LSD radix sort</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Binary Search i32</td>\n<td><span id=\"algobsearchi32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoBsearchI32(arr, len, k)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"bsearchi32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.bsearchI32(...)</code></td>\n<td>Binary search (returns -1 if not found)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Binary Search u32</td>\n<td><span id=\"algobsearchu32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoBsearchU32(arr, len, k)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"bsearchu32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.bsearchU32(...)</code></td>\n<td>Binary search on unsigned array</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Shuffle Array</td>\n<td><span id=\"algoshuffle\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoShuffle(base, n, sz)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"shuffle\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.shuffle(...)</code></td>\n<td>In-place Fisher-Yates shuffle</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Reverse Array</td>\n<td><span id=\"algoreverse\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AlgoReverse(base, n, sz)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"reverse\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>algo.reverse(...)</code></td>\n<td>In-place element reversal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Init PRNG</td>\n<td><span id=\"randinit\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>RandInit(rng, seed)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"init\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>rng.init(rng, seed)</code></td>\n<td>Seed Xoshiro256** generator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Random u64</td>\n<td><span id=\"randu64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>RandU64(rng)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"u64_\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>rng.u64_(rng)</code></td>\n<td>Generate 64-bit unsigned random value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Random f64</td>\n<td><span id=\"randf64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>RandF64(rng)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"f64_\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>rng.f64_(rng)</code></td>\n<td>Generate [0.0, 1.0) double float</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Random Range</td>\n<td><span id=\"randrange\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>RandRange(rng, min, max)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"range\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>rng.range(rng, min, max)</code></td>\n<td>Uniform integer in [min, max]</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Telemetry &amp; Sensor Sorting</strong>: Sort 1,000,000 integer readings in sub-millisecond time using <code>AlgoRadixSortU32</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Monte Carlo Simulations</strong>: Generate billions of pseudorandom numbers per second using thread-local <code>Rng</code> states.</li>\n<li><strong>Database Index Lookup</strong>: Search binary sorted keys with $O(\\log N)$ guarantees.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"sorting\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"with\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"anonymous\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"lambda\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-sorting-with-anonymous-lambda\"><a href=\"#example-sorting-with-anonymous-lambda\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: Sorting with Anonymous Lambda</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> id;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> score;\n} <span class=\"tok-func\">Player</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> rank_players(<span class=\"tok-func\">Player</span> *players, <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> count) {\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">AlgoSort</span>(players, count, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">Player</span>), <span class=\"tok-func\">Lambda</span>(<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *a, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *b), {\n        <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> diff = ((<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-func\">Player</span> *)b)-&gt;score - ((<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-func\">Player</span> *)a)-&gt;score;\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> (diff &gt; <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>) - (diff &lt; <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>);\n    }));\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Array Monotonicity in <code>BinarySearch</code></strong>: <code>AlgoBsearchI32</code> requires the input array to be sorted in ascending order beforehand.</li>\n<li><strong>Zero Seed in PRNG</strong>: Do not seed <code>Rng</code> with all zeros (<code>seed = 0</code>), as Xoshiro256** requires at least one non-zero state bit. <code>RandInit</code> automatically mixes non-zero bits via SplitMix64 if seed is 0.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_math": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_math\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"simd\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"linear\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"algebra\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"geometry\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-math-simd-linear-algebra-amp-geometry\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-math-simd-linear-algebra-amp-geometry\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_math (SIMD Linear Algebra &amp; Geometry)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_math</code> module provides 2D/3D/4D single-precision vectors (<code>Vec2</code>, <code>Vec3</code>, <code>Vec4</code>) and SIMD-accelerated 4x4 column-major matrices (<code>Mat4</code>) with AVX/SSE vectorization, perspective projections, Euler rotations, and fast inverse square root.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Vec3</span> eye = cp_vec3(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">5</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">10</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Vec3</span> target = cp_vec3(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Vec3</span> up = cp_vec3(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span> view = <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4LookAt</span>(eye, target, up);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span> proj = <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4Perspective</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">CP_DEG2RAD</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">60</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>), <span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span> / <span class=\"tok-number\">9</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">1f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1000</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span> vp = <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4Mul</span>(&amp;proj, &amp;view);\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">f32</span> inv = <span class=\"tok-func\">MathFastInvSqrt</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">25</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// ~0.20</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layouts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"vec2\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"vec3\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"vec4\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"mat4\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layouts-vec2-vec3-vec4-mat4\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layouts-vec2-vec3-vec4-mat4\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layouts: <code>Vec2</code>, <code>Vec3</code>, <code>Vec4</code>, <code>Mat4</code></h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> { <span class=\"tok-type\">f32</span> x, y; } <span class=\"tok-func\">Vec2</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> { <span class=\"tok-type\">f32</span> x, y, z; } <span class=\"tok-func\">Vec3</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_ALIGN</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>) <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> { <span class=\"tok-type\">f32</span> x, y, z, w; } <span class=\"tok-func\">Vec4</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_ALIGN</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>) <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_mat4 {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">f32</span> m[<span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>];\n} <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SIMD Alignment</strong>: <code>Vec4</code> and <code>Mat4</code> are aligned to 16 bytes (<code>_Alignas(16)</code>), allowing the compiler to emit direct SSE <code>_mm_load_ps</code> / <code>_mm_mul_ps</code> or AVX <code>_mm256</code> instructions without unaligned penalty.</li>\n<li><strong>Column-Major Matrix Format</strong>: Array layout matches standard OpenGL, Vulkan, and Metal GPU shaders (<code>m[col * 4 + row]</code>), allowing direct DMA transfer to GPU buffers.</li>\n<li><strong>Fast Inverse Square Root (<code>MathFastInvSqrt</code>)</strong>: Classic IEEE 754 bit-hack approximation using constant <code>0x5f3759df</code> and a single Newton-Raphson refinement pass.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Vec2 / Vec3 / Vec4</th>\n<th>Mat4 Multiplication</th>\n<th>Mat4 Inversion</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Time Complexity</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ scalar</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ SIMD unrolled (16 FMAs)</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ Cramer's rule SIMD</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Allocation</strong></td>\n<td>0B (value types)</td>\n<td>0B (registers/stack)</td>\n<td>0B (registers/stack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Vectorization</strong></td>\n<td>Auto-vectorized</td>\n<td>SSE / AVX unrolled loops</td>\n<td>SSE / AVX unrolled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Pure functions</td>\n<td>Pure functions</td>\n<td>Pure functions</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Vector 2D</td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_vec2\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_vec2(x, y)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Construct Vec2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vector 3D</td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_vec3\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_vec3(x, y, z)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Construct Vec3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vector 4D</td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_vec4\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_vec4(x, y, z, w)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Construct 16-byte aligned Vec4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cross Product</td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_vec3_cross\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_vec3_cross(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>3D vector cross product</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Normalize</td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_vec3_norm\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_vec3_norm(v)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Normalize 3D vector to unit length</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Identity Matrix</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4identity\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4Identity()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"identity\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.identity()</code></td>\n<td>4x4 Identity matrix</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Translation</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4translate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4Translate(x, y, z)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"translate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.translate(x, y, z)</code></td>\n<td>Translate transform matrix</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scale Matrix</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4scale\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4Scale(x, y, z)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"scale\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.scale(x, y, z)</code></td>\n<td>Scaling transform matrix</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rotation X</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4rotatex\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4RotateX(rad)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"rotatex\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.rotateX(rad)</code></td>\n<td>Rotation around X axis in radians</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rotation Y</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4rotatey\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4RotateY(rad)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"rotatey\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.rotateY(rad)</code></td>\n<td>Rotation around Y axis in radians</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rotation Z</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4rotatez\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4RotateZ(rad)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"rotatez\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.rotateZ(rad)</code></td>\n<td>Rotation around Z axis in radians</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Perspective</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4perspective\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4Perspective(fov, a, n, f)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"perspective\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.perspective(...)</code></td>\n<td>Perspective projection matrix</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Look-At</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4lookat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4LookAt(eye, center, up)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"lookat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.lookAt(...)</code></td>\n<td>Camera view matrix</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Matrix Multiply</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4mul\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4Mul(a, b)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"mul\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.mul(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>SIMD matrix multiplication</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transform Vec4</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4mulvec4\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4MulVec4(m, v)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"mulvec4\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.mulVec4(m, v)</code></td>\n<td>Multiply matrix by column vector</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Matrix Invert</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4invert\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4Invert(src, dst)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"invert\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.invert(src, dst)</code></td>\n<td>Matrix inversion (returns false if singular)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Matrix Transpose</td>\n<td><span id=\"mat4transpose\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Mat4Transpose(m)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"transpose\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.transpose(m)</code></td>\n<td>Column/row matrix transpose</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fast Inv Sqrt</td>\n<td><span id=\"mathfastinvsqrt\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MathFastInvSqrt(x)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"fastinvsqrt\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.fastInvSqrt(x)</code></td>\n<td>1 / sqrt(x) fast approximation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Clamp</td>\n<td><span id=\"clamp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Clamp(val, min, max)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"clamp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.clamp(...)</code></td>\n<td>Scalar range clamping</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lerp</td>\n<td><span id=\"lerp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Lerp(a, b, t)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"lerp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>math.lerp(a, b, t)</code></td>\n<td>Linear interpolation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>3D Graphics &amp; Game Engines</strong>: Compute Model-View-Projection (MVP) matrices for rendering pipelines.</li>\n<li><strong>Robotics &amp; Kinematics</strong>: Calculate forward and inverse kinematics using translation and rotation matrices.</li>\n<li><strong>Physics Simulations</strong>: Fast collision detection and ray-plane intersections using vector dot and cross products.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"mvp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"transformation\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-mvp-transformation\"><a href=\"#example-mvp-transformation\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: MVP Transformation</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Vec4</span> transform_world_point(<span class=\"tok-func\">Vec3</span> point, <span class=\"tok-func\">Vec3</span> camera_pos) {\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span> model = <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4Translate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span> view = <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4LookAt</span>(camera_pos, cp_vec3(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>), cp_vec3(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>));\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span> proj = <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4Perspective</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">CP_DEG2RAD</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">60</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>), <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">777f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">1f</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">100</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span> mv = <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4Mul</span>(&amp;view, &amp;model);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4</span> mvp = <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4Mul</span>(&amp;proj, &amp;mv);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Vec4</span> p = cp_vec4(point.x, point.y, point.z, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-func\">Mat4MulVec4</span>(&amp;mvp, p);\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Singular Matrices in <code>Mat4Invert</code></strong>: If a matrix determinant is near zero ($|\\det| &lt; 10^{-6}$), <code>Mat4Invert</code> returns <code>false</code> and leaves <code>dst</code> untouched. Always verify the return code.</li>\n<li><strong>Radian Units</strong>: All trigonometric and rotation functions expect angles in <strong>radians</strong>. Use <code>CP_DEG2RAD(degrees)</code> to convert from degrees.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_thread": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_thread\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"concurrency\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"synchronization\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-thread-concurrency-amp-synchronization\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-thread-concurrency-amp-synchronization\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_thread (Concurrency &amp; Synchronization)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_thread</code> module provides pre-warmed worker thread pooling (<code>ThreadPool</code>), work-sharing loops (<code>ParallelFor</code>), scoped RAII mutex locks (<code>ScopedLock</code>, <code>WithLock</code>), condition variables (<code>CondVar</code>), and C11 atomic primitives without external runtime dependencies (zero OpenMP required).</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">ThreadPool</span> *pool = <span class=\"tok-func\">ThreadPoolCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Auto-detect CPU cores</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Asynchronous Task with Closure */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ThreadPoolSubmit</span>(pool, <span class=\"tok-func\">Lambda</span>(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg), {\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Task executing on background worker!\\n&quot;</span>);\n}), <span class=\"tok-type\">NULL</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Parallel-For Range Partitioning with Barrier Sync */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ParallelFor</span>(pool, <span class=\"tok-number\">1000000</span>, <span class=\"tok-func\">Lambda</span>(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>, (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> start, <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> end, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg), {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *arr = (<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *)arg;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> i = start; i &lt; end; i++) arr[i] *= <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0f</span>;\n}), data);\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ThreadPoolDestroy</span>(pool);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"threadpool\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_threadpool_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layout-threadpool-cp-threadpool-t\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layout-threadpool-cp-threadpool-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layout: <code>ThreadPool</code> (<code>cp_threadpool_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> (*fn)(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_pool_task_t</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_threadpool {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_thread_t</span> *threads;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> num_threads;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_pool_task_t</span> *queue;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> queue_capacity;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> queue_head;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> queue_tail;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> queue_count;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> active_workers;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_mutex_t</span> lock;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_cond_t</span> not_empty;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_cond_t</span> not_full;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_cond_t</span> all_idle;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> shutdown;\n};</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Pre-Warmed Workers</strong>: Threads are instantiated once during <code>ThreadPoolCreate</code> and remain idle on <code>cp_cond_wait(&amp;pool-&gt;not_empty, &amp;pool-&gt;lock)</code> when no work is pending, eliminating <code>pthread_create</code> overhead.</li>\n<li><strong>Bounded Circular Queue</strong>: Prevents unbounded memory growth. If the queue is full, <code>ThreadPoolSubmit</code> blocks on <code>not_full</code> until capacity opens up.</li>\n<li><strong>ParallelFor Calling Thread Participation</strong>: When executing <code>ParallelFor</code>, the calling thread executes the final range slice directly on the current core while worker threads process the other slices in parallel, avoiding CPU core starvation and eliminating thread hopping.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"raii\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"scoped\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"locks\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-raii-scoped-locks\"><a href=\"#2-2-raii-scoped-locks\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 RAII Scoped Locks</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> ScopedLock(m_ptr) \\\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">pthread_mutex_t</span> *<span class=\"tok-func\">CP_CONCAT</span>(_scoped_mtx_, __LINE__) __attribute__((cleanup(_cp_scoped_mutex_unlock), unused)) = \\\n        (pthread_mutex_lock((<span class=\"tok-type\">pthread_mutex_t</span>*)(m_ptr)), (<span class=\"tok-type\">pthread_mutex_t</span>*)(m_ptr))\n\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> WithLock(m_ptr) \\\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> _lock_done_ = (pthread_mutex_lock((<span class=\"tok-type\">pthread_mutex_t</span>*)(m_ptr)), <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>); \\\n         !_lock_done_; \\\n         pthread_mutex_unlock((<span class=\"tok-type\">pthread_mutex_t</span>*)(m_ptr)), _lock_done_ = <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Completely eliminates mutex leak deadlocks on unexpected early returns or goto labels.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>ThreadPool</th>\n<th>Mutex / ScopedLock</th>\n<th>Atomic Primitives</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Dispatch Latency</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ task queue insertion</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ fast-path futex lock</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ hardware instruction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Worker Synchronization</strong></td>\n<td>Condition variable signaling</td>\n<td>OS futex / kernel sleep</td>\n<td>Hardware cache coherence (<code>LOCK</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Allocation</strong></td>\n<td>Pre-allocated during init</td>\n<td>0 heap allocations</td>\n<td>0 heap allocations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>External Dependencies</strong></td>\n<td>Standard <code>libpthread</code></td>\n<td>Standard <code>libpthread</code></td>\n<td>Inlined GCC/Clang builtins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Safe for concurrent submits</td>\n<td>Thread-safe mutual exclusion</td>\n<td>Lock-free sequential consistency</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Create Pool</td>\n<td><span id=\"threadpoolcreate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ThreadPoolCreate(threads, cap)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"create\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>threadpool.create(...)</code></td>\n<td>Initialize pre-warmed pool (0 = auto cores)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Submit Task</td>\n<td><span id=\"threadpoolsubmit\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ThreadPoolSubmit(pool, fn, arg)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"submit\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>threadpool.submit(...)</code></td>\n<td>Blocking submit (blocks if queue is full)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Try Submit</td>\n<td><span id=\"threadpooltrysubmit\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ThreadPoolTrySubmit(p, fn, arg)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"trysubmit\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>threadpool.trySubmit(...)</code></td>\n<td>Non-blocking submit (returns false if full)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Parallel-For</td>\n<td><span id=\"parallelfor\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ParallelFor(pool, count, fn, arg)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"parallelfor\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>threadpool.parallelFor(...)</code></td>\n<td>Parallel range processing with barrier sync</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Parallel Vector</td>\n<td><span id=\"vecparallelmap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>VecParallelMap(pool, vec, body)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>In-place parallel dynamic array mapping</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wait Pool</td>\n<td><span id=\"threadpoolwait\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ThreadPoolWait(pool)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"wait\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>threadpool.wait(pool)</code></td>\n<td>Block until all queued/active tasks finish</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Destroy Pool</td>\n<td><span id=\"threadpooldestroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ThreadPoolDestroy(pool)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"destroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>threadpool.destroy(pool)</code></td>\n<td>Join workers and free resources</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scoped Lock</td>\n<td><span id=\"scopedlock\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ScopedLock(&amp;mutex)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>RAII block auto-unlock</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>With Lock</td>\n<td><span id=\"withlock\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>WithLock(&amp;mutex) { ... }</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Synchronized execution block</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Atomic Add</td>\n<td><span id=\"atomicadd\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AtomicAdd(ptr, val)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Inlined atomic increment/add</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Atomic Store</td>\n<td><span id=\"atomicstore\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>AtomicStore(ptr, val)</code></td>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>Sequentially consistent atomic store</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Parallel Raytracing &amp; Image Filters</strong>: Partition pixel scanlines across CPU cores using <code>ParallelFor</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Asynchronous I/O Dispatch</strong>: Offload slow disk writes and database queries to the <code>ThreadPool</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Deadlock-Free State Protection</strong>: Guard shared hash tables and caches using <code>ScopedLock(&amp;m)</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"multi\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"core\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"vector\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"computation\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-multi-core-vector-computation\"><a href=\"#example-multi-core-vector-computation\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: Multi-Core Vector Computation</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> parallel_audio_normalize(<span class=\"tok-type\">ThreadPool</span> *pool, <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *samples, <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> count) {\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Process 1,000,000 audio samples partitioned evenly across all CPU cores</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">ParallelFor</span>(pool, count, <span class=\"tok-func\">Lambda</span>(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>, (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> start, <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> end, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *arg), {\n        <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *buf = (<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> *)arg;\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> i = start; i &lt; end; i++) {\n            buf[i] = tanhf(buf[i] * <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">5f</span>);\n        }\n    }), samples);\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Recursive <code>ParallelFor</code></strong>: Do not invoke <code>ParallelFor</code> from inside a task that is itself already running on a thread pool worker, as this can cause worker starvation if all threads block waiting for sub-tasks.</li>\n<li><strong>Task Queue Saturation</strong>: Default queue capacity is 4096. If you submit 100,000 independent tasks via <code>ThreadPoolSubmit</code> without waiting, the submitting thread will block until space opens up in the ring queue. Use <code>ParallelFor</code> instead of submitting single-item tasks.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_net": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_net\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"networking\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"industrial\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"fieldbuses\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-net-networking-amp-industrial-fieldbuses\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-net-networking-amp-industrial-fieldbuses\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_net (Networking &amp; Industrial Fieldbuses)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_net</code> module provides non-blocking TCP and UDP socket wrappers, high-throughput Modbus RTU/TCP industrial framing with hardware-lookup CRC16, and Linux SocketCAN framing.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Ergonomic TCP Request One-Liner */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> response[<span class=\"tok-number\">512</span>];\n<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> resp_len = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> ok = <span class=\"tok-func\">NetTcpRequest</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;127.0.0.1&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">8080</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;GET /status&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">11</span>, response, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(response), &amp;resp_len, <span class=\"tok-number\">2000</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Modbus CRC16 Calculation */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> modbus_frame[] = { <span class=\"tok-number\">0x01</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0x03</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0x00</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0x00</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0x00</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0x0A</span> };\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u16</span> crc = <span class=\"tok-func\">ModbusCrc16</span>(modbus_frame, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(modbus_frame));</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"socket\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"descriptors\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-socket-descriptors\"><a href=\"#2-1-socket-descriptors\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Socket Descriptors</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">Socket</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> CP_INVALID_SOCKET (-1)</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Standard POSIX file descriptors configured for non-blocking asynchronous event loops (<code>O_NONBLOCK</code>).</li>\n<li>Built-in socket options: <code>SO_REUSEADDR</code> for instant server restarts without <code>EADDRINUSE</code>, and <code>TCP_NODELAY</code> to disable Nagle's algorithm for sub-millisecond RPC latency.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"industrial\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"modbus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"can\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"structures\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-industrial-modbus-amp-can-structures\"><a href=\"#2-2-industrial-modbus-amp-can-structures\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Industrial Modbus &amp; CAN Structures</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u32</span> can_id;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> len;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> data[<span class=\"tok-number\">8</span>];\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_can_frame_t</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Modbus RTU framing with pre-calculated table-driven CRC16 computation (polynomial <code>0xA001</code>, initial value <code>0xFFFF</code>), processing frames in a single memory pass.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>TCP / UDP Sockets</th>\n<th>Modbus CRC16</th>\n<th>SocketCAN</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>I/O Latency</strong></td>\n<td>Non-blocking (kernel poll)</td>\n<td>Sub-microsecond (table lookup)</td>\n<td>Direct kernel socket</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Allocation</strong></td>\n<td>0 heap allocations</td>\n<td>0B (static table)</td>\n<td>0 heap allocations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Timeout Handling</strong></td>\n<td>Millisecond precision (<code>poll</code>)</td>\n<td>Pure calculation</td>\n<td>Millisecond precision</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Thread-safe socket descriptors</td>\n<td>Pure function</td>\n<td>Thread-safe descriptors</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>TCP Connect</td>\n<td><span id=\"nettcpconnect\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetTcpConnect(h, port, to_ms)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"tcpconnect\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.tcpConnect(...)</code></td>\n<td>Connect to remote TCP host with timeout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TCP Listen</td>\n<td><span id=\"nettcplisten\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetTcpListen(addr, port, b)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"tcplisten\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.tcpListen(...)</code></td>\n<td>Bind and listen for incoming connections</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TCP Accept</td>\n<td><span id=\"nettcpaccept\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetTcpAccept(fd, ip, sz, &amp;p)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"tcpaccept\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.tcpAccept(...)</code></td>\n<td>Accept client, extract IP and port</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TCP Request</td>\n<td><span id=\"nettcprequest\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetTcpRequest(h, p, req, ...)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"tcprequest\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.tcpRequest(...)</code></td>\n<td>One-liner request/response client</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Send All</td>\n<td><span id=\"netsendall\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetSendAll(fd, buf, len, to)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sendall\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.sendAll(...)</code></td>\n<td>Reliably send exact byte stream</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Receive</td>\n<td><span id=\"netrecv\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetRecv(fd, buf, cap, to)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"recv\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.recv(...)</code></td>\n<td>Non-blocking read with timeout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>UDP Bind</td>\n<td><span id=\"netudpbind\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetUdpBind(addr, port)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"udpbind\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.udpBind(...)</code></td>\n<td>Bind local UDP socket</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>UDP Send To</td>\n<td><span id=\"netudpsendto\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetUdpSendTo(fd, h, p, d, l)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"udpsendto\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.udpSendTo(...)</code></td>\n<td>Send UDP datagram to target</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>UDP Send</td>\n<td><span id=\"netudpsend\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetUdpSend(h, p, d, l)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"udpsend\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.udpSend(...)</code></td>\n<td>One-liner UDP datagram dispatch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Close Socket</td>\n<td><span id=\"netclose\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>NetClose(fd)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"close\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>net.close(fd)</code></td>\n<td>Graceful socket shutdown and close</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Modbus CRC16</td>\n<td><span id=\"modbuscrc16\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ModbusCrc16(buf, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"crc16\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>modbus.crc16(...)</code></td>\n<td>256-word table CRC16 calculation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pack Read Holding</td>\n<td><span id=\"modbusrtupackreadholding\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ModbusRtuPackReadHolding(...)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"packreadholding\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>modbus.packReadHolding(...)</code></td>\n<td>Pack Modbus function code 0x03</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CAN Open</td>\n<td><span id=\"cansocketopen\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>CanSocketOpen(ifname)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"open\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>can.open(...)</code></td>\n<td>Open Linux SocketCAN interface</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CAN Send</td>\n<td><span id=\"cansend\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>CanSend(fd, frame)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"send\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>can.send(...)</code></td>\n<td>Transmit CAN 2.0A/B frame</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Microservice RPC Clients</strong>: Issue fast non-blocking TCP queries using <code>NetTcpRequest</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Industrial Automation &amp; SCADA</strong>: Communicate with PLCs, VFDs, and sensors via Modbus RTU/TCP.</li>\n<li><strong>Automotive &amp; Telematics</strong>: Read vehicle sensors via Linux SocketCAN (<code>vcan0</code> / <code>can0</code>).</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"udp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"telemetry\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"dispatch\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-udp-telemetry-dispatch\"><a href=\"#example-udp-telemetry-dispatch\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: UDP Telemetry Dispatch</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> broadcast_telemetry(<span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> temp, <span class=\"tok-type\">float</span> pressure) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> payload[<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span>];\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> len = snprintf(payload, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(payload), <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;{\\&quot;</span>temp\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;:%.2f,\\&quot;</span>pres\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;:%.2f}&quot;</span>, temp, pressure);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">// One-liner: sends UDP datagram without managing socket lifecycle manually</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">NetUdpSend</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;192.168.1.255&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">9000</span>, payload, (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span>)len);\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Platform Support for CAN</strong>: <code>CanSocketOpen</code> requires a Linux kernel with <code>AF_CAN</code> support enabled. On macOS and Windows, CAN APIs return error codes.</li>\n<li><strong>TCP Request Buffering</strong>: <code>NetTcpRequest</code> reads up to <code>resp_buf_cap</code> bytes. If the server response exceeds the buffer capacity, data is truncated to prevent buffer overflows.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_tui": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_tui\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"differential\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"terminal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"engine\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-tui-differential-terminal-ui-engine\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-tui-differential-terminal-ui-engine\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_tui (Differential Terminal UI Engine)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_tui</code> module provides a double-buffered ANSI virtual terminal engine capable of 75,000 FPS differential rendering, reducing terminal I/O bandwidth by up to 95% by flushing only dirty cells.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Tui</span> *tui = <span class=\"tok-func\">TuiInit</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Auto-detect terminal dimensions</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">TuiClear</span>(tui, <span class=\"tok-func\">TUI_COLOR_BLACK</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">TuiDrawBox</span>(tui, <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">10</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot; System Monitor &quot;</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">TuiPrint</span>(tui, <span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;CPU Usage: 12.4%&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-func\">TUI_COLOR_BRIGHT_GREEN</span>, <span class=\"tok-func\">TUI_COLOR_BLACK</span>, <span class=\"tok-func\">TUI_ATTR_BOLD</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">TuiFlush</span>(tui); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Emits sub-microsecond diffs to stdout</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">TuiShutdown</span>(tui); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Restores terminal mode and cursor</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"tui\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_tui_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"and\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"tuicell\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_tui_cell_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layout-tui-cp-tui-t-and-tuicell-cp-tui-cell-t\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layout-tui-cp-tui-t-and-tuicell-cp-tui-cell-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layout: <code>Tui</code> (<code>cp_tui_t</code>) and <code>TuiCell</code> (<code>cp_tui_cell_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> glyph[<span class=\"tok-number\">8</span>]; <span class=\"tok-comment\">/**&lt; UTF-8 multi-byte or ASCII glyph */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> fg;         <span class=\"tok-comment\">/**&lt; Foreground ANSI color */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> bg;         <span class=\"tok-comment\">/**&lt; Background ANSI color */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> attrs;      <span class=\"tok-comment\">/**&lt; Attributes bitmask (bold, dim, underline, reverse) */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> _pad;\n} <span class=\"tok-func\">TuiCell</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_tui {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> width;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> height;\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">TuiCell</span> *front_buffer;\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">TuiCell</span> *back_buffer;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *out_buffer;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> out_cap;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> out_len;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> is_headless;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> raw_mode_active;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> termios orig_termios;\n} <span class=\"tok-func\">Tui</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Differential Screen Flush</strong>: Compares <code>front_buffer</code> (currently displayed on terminal) against <code>back_buffer</code> (what you just drew). Only differing cells generate ANSI escape sequences (<code>\\x1b[row;colH\\x1b[attr;fg;bgm&lt;glyph&gt;</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Zero Redraw Flicker</strong>: Eliminates full-screen clears (<code>\\x1b[2J</code>), resulting in buttery-smooth terminal dashboards and interactive UIs.</li>\n<li><strong>Headless Mode (<code>TuiCreate(w, h, true)</code>)</strong>: Allocates buffers in memory without switching the physical terminal to raw mode. Ideal for unit tests, CI/CD pipelines, and server-side screenshot rendering.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Guarantee</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Flush Throughput</strong></td>\n<td>~75,000 FPS (13 \u00b5s per frame)</td>\n<td>Bounded only by terminal emulator I/O</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>I/O Reduction</strong></td>\n<td>-93% to -98% fewer ANSI bytes</td>\n<td>Only dirty cells are emitted</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Allocation</strong></td>\n<td>Pre-allocated during <code>TuiInit</code></td>\n<td>2 matrix buffers + 1 write buffer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Terminal Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Automatic cursor &amp; raw mode cleanup</td>\n<td>Restores original termios on shutdown</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Thread-confined</td>\n<td>Must be driven by a dedicated render thread</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Init Physical TUI</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuiinit\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiInit(w, h)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"init\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.init(w, h)</code></td>\n<td>Auto-detects terminal size (0, 0)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create Headless</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuicreate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiCreate(w, h, headless)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"create\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.create(...)</code></td>\n<td>Create off-screen rendering engine</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Shutdown TUI</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuishutdown\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiShutdown(tui)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"shutdown\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.shutdown(tui)</code></td>\n<td>Restore terminal raw mode and cursor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Clear Buffer</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuiclear\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiClear(tui, bg_color)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"clear\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.clear(tui, bg)</code></td>\n<td>Fill back buffer with background color</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Set Single Cell</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuisetcell\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiSetCell(tui, x, y, g, ...)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"setcell\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.setCell(...)</code></td>\n<td>Place glyph at coordinate with attributes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Print Text</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuiprint\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiPrint(tui, x, y, str, ...)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"print\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.print(...)</code></td>\n<td>Print string with color and clipping</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Draw Box</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuidrawbox\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiDrawBox(tui, x, y, w, h, t)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"drawbox\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.drawBox(...)</code></td>\n<td>Rounded Unicode bordered container</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Flush Diff</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuiflush\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiFlush(tui)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"flush\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.flush(tui)</code></td>\n<td>Differential render to stdout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read Key</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuireadkey\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiReadKey(tui, timeout_ms)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"readkey\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.readKey(...)</code></td>\n<td>Non-blocking key parser</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Interactive Menu</td>\n<td><span id=\"tuimenu\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TuiMenu(tui, title, items, n)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"menu\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>tui.menu(...)</code></td>\n<td>Blocking selection menu</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Server Telemetry Dashboards</strong>: Display CPU, RAM, disk, and network stats at 60 FPS with negligible CPU usage.</li>\n<li><strong>Interactive CLI Installers</strong>: Prompt users with menus and dialog boxes.</li>\n<li><strong>Embedded Hardware Terminals</strong>: Low-bandwidth UART serial console displays.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"interactive\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"menu\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"selection\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-interactive-menu-selection\"><a href=\"#example-interactive-menu-selection\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: Interactive Menu Selection</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> choose_deployment_target(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Tui</span> *tui = <span class=\"tok-func\">TuiInit</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *options[] = { <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Staging (Local)&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Production (US-East)&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Disaster Recovery&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Cancel&quot;</span> };\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Renders interactive menu with arrow-key navigation and Enter selection</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> selection = <span class=\"tok-func\">TuiMenu</span>(tui, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot; Select Deployment Target &quot;</span>, options, <span class=\"tok-number\">4</span>);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">TuiShutdown</span>(tui);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> selection;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>UTF-8 Multi-Byte Glyphs</strong>: Each <code>TuiCell</code> reserves 8 bytes for glyph representation, accommodating UTF-8 sequences (including box-drawing characters and icons). Combining characters requiring wide double-width font layout (e.g. CJK ideographs) take 2 horizontal cells.</li>\n<li><strong>Terminal Resize Handling</strong>: If the physical terminal window is resized, call <code>TuiShutdown</code> and re-initialize <code>TuiInit(0, 0)</code> to adapt to new rows/columns.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_hash": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_hash\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"hashing\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"subsystem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-hash-hashing-subsystem\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-hash-hashing-subsystem\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_hash (Hashing Subsystem)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_hash</code> subsystem delivers both ultra-high-throughput non-cryptographic hash functions for hash tables and checksums, and a clean FIPS 180-4 compliant SHA-256 implementation with zero external dependencies.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Ultra-Fast 64-bit Mixer Hash (&lt; 1 ns/byte, &gt; 3.5 GB/s) */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *key = <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;session_token_991823&quot;</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> h64 = <span class=\"tok-func\">Hash64</span>(key, strlen(key));\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Standard 32-bit FNV-1a */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u32</span> h32 = <span class=\"tok-func\">HashFnv1a32</span>(key, strlen(key));\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. Cryptographic FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> digest[<span class=\"tok-number\">32</span>];\n<span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> hex[<span class=\"tok-number\">65</span>];\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Sha256</span>(key, strlen(key), digest);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">Sha256Hex</span>(digest, hex);\nprintf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;SHA-256: %s\\n&quot;</span>, hex);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"fast\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"non\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cryptographic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"mixer\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"hash64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_hash64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-fast-non-cryptographic-mixer-hash64-cp-hash64\"><a href=\"#2-1-fast-non-cryptographic-mixer-hash64-cp-hash64\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Fast Non-Cryptographic Mixer: <code>Hash64</code> (<code>cp_hash64</code>)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Employs an unrolled multiply-shift-xor mixing pipeline based on 64-bit golden ratio constants.</li>\n<li>Processes 8-byte words per step with residual handling for trailing bytes.</li>\n<li>Passes standard Avalanche tests with uniform distribution across 64-bit hash table buckets.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"fnv\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"hashfnv1a32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"hashfnv1a64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-fnv-1a-hashfnv1a32-amp-hashfnv1a64\"><a href=\"#2-2-fnv-1a-hashfnv1a32-amp-hashfnv1a64\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 FNV-1a: <code>HashFnv1a32</code> &amp; <code>HashFnv1a64</code></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Standard Fowler-Noll-Vo algorithm.</li>\n<li>Initialized with offset basis (<code>2166136261u</code> for 32-bit, <code>14695981039346656037ull</code> for 64-bit).</li>\n<li>Multiplies by FNV prime per byte and XORs with byte payload.</li>\n<li>Minimal code footprint, optimal for short strings and identifiers.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"cryptographic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"sha\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"256\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"sha256\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_sha256\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-3-cryptographic-sha-256-sha256-cp-sha256\"><a href=\"#2-3-cryptographic-sha-256-sha256-cp-sha256\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.3 Cryptographic SHA-256: <code>Sha256</code> (<code>cp_sha256</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u32</span> state[<span class=\"tok-number\">8</span>];\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> count;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> buffer[<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span>];\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_sha256_ctx_t</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Fully compliant with NIST FIPS PUB 180-4.</li>\n<li>Processes 512-bit message blocks with 64 constant transformation rounds.</li>\n<li>Supports both incremental streaming (<code>Sha256Init</code> -&gt; <code>Sha256Update</code> -&gt; <code>Sha256Final</code>) and direct one-shot evaluation (<code>Sha256</code>).</li>\n<li>Converts 32-byte binary digest to lowercase hexadecimal string (<code>Sha256Hex</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Output Size</th>\n<th>Throughput</th>\n<th>Cryptographic Security</th>\n<th>Heap Allocations</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"hash64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Hash64</code></td>\n<td>64 bits</td>\n<td>~3.8 GB/s (memory bound)</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"hashfnv1a64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>HashFnv1a64</code></td>\n<td>64 bits</td>\n<td>~1.2 GB/s</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"hashfnv1a32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>HashFnv1a32</code></td>\n<td>32 bits</td>\n<td>~1.2 GB/s</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"sha256\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Sha256</code></td>\n<td>256 bits</td>\n<td>~350 MB/s</td>\n<td>Yes (Pre-image resistant)</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Fast 64-bit Hash</td>\n<td><span id=\"hash64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Hash64(data, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"u64_hash\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>hash_api.u64_hash(data, len)</code></td>\n<td>High-throughput non-cryptographic 64-bit mixer hash</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FNV-1a 32-bit</td>\n<td><span id=\"hashfnv1a32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>HashFnv1a32(data, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"fnv1a32\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>hash_api.fnv1a32(data, len)</code></td>\n<td>Standard 32-bit Fowler-Noll-Vo hash</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FNV-1a 64-bit</td>\n<td><span id=\"hashfnv1a64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>HashFnv1a64(data, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"fnv1a64\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>hash_api.fnv1a64(data, len)</code></td>\n<td>Standard 64-bit Fowler-Noll-Vo hash</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>One-Shot SHA-256</td>\n<td><span id=\"sha256\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Sha256(data, len, out)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sha256\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>hash_api.sha256(data, len, out)</code></td>\n<td>Compute NIST FIPS 180-4 32-byte hash digest</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SHA-256 to Hex</td>\n<td><span id=\"sha256hex\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Sha256Hex(in, out_hex)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sha256hex\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>hash_api.sha256Hex(in, out_hex)</code></td>\n<td>Format 32-byte hash into 64-character null-terminated hex</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Init SHA-256 Ctx</td>\n<td><span id=\"sha256init\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Sha256Init(ctx)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_sha256_init\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_sha256_init(ctx)</code></td>\n<td>Initialize incremental SHA-256 context</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Update SHA-256</td>\n<td><span id=\"sha256update\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Sha256Update(ctx, buf, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_sha256_update\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_sha256_update(ctx, buf, len)</code></td>\n<td>Stream bytes into SHA-256 context</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Finalize SHA-256</td>\n<td><span id=\"sha256final\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>Sha256Final(ctx, out)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"cp_sha256_final\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>cp_sha256_final(ctx, out)</code></td>\n<td>Complete padding and emit 32-byte digest</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Hash Table Keying</strong>: Use <code>Hash64</code> inside custom hash tables or <code>HashMap</code> for minimal collision rates and high throughput.</li>\n<li><strong>File Integrity Verification</strong>: Hash incoming firmware or file buffers with <code>Sha256</code> and compare checksums against authoritative sources.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Deduplication</strong>: Identify identical data chunks in network transmission by maintaining a set of SHA-256 hashes.</li>\n<li><strong>Fast String Partitioning</strong>: Partition short identifiers across thread worker queues using <code>HashFnv1a32(id, len) % worker_count</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"compilable\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-compilable-example\"><a href=\"#6-complete-compilable-example\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete Compilable Example</h2>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;assert.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> main(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *msg = <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog&quot;</span>;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> len = strlen(msg);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Fast mixer hash */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> h64 = hash_api.u64_hash(msg, len);\n    assert(h64 != <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. One-shot SHA-256 */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> digest[<span class=\"tok-number\">32</span>];\n    hash_api.sha256(msg, len, digest);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> hex[<span class=\"tok-number\">65</span>];\n    hash_api.sha256Hex(digest, hex);\n    assert(strcmp(hex, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;d7a8fbb307d7809469ca9abcb0082e4f8d5651e46d3cdb762d02d0bf37c9e592&quot;</span>) == <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Message: \\&quot;</span>%s\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;\\nSHA-256: %s\\n&quot;</span>, msg, hex);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. Incremental streaming SHA-256 */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_sha256_ctx_t</span> ctx;\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Sha256Init</span>(&amp;ctx);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Sha256Update</span>(&amp;ctx, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;The quick brown &quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Sha256Update</span>(&amp;ctx, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;fox jumps over the lazy dog&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">27</span>);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u8</span> stream_digest[<span class=\"tok-number\">32</span>];\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Sha256Final</span>(&amp;ctx, stream_digest);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> stream_hex[<span class=\"tok-number\">65</span>];\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">Sha256Hex</span>(stream_digest, stream_hex);\n    assert(strcmp(hex, stream_hex) == <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"edge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Edge Cases</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Non-Cryptographic Collisions</strong>: <code>Hash64</code> and <code>HashFnv1a</code> are strictly designed for hash tables, bloom filters, and checksums. They must not be used for cryptographic signatures, passwords, or security authentication.</li>\n<li><strong>Hex Buffer Sizing</strong>: <code>Sha256Hex</code> requires an output buffer of at least 65 bytes (<code>32 * 2 + 1</code> for null-terminator). Supplying smaller buffers causes memory corruption.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_map": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_map\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"open\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"addressing\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"hash\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"table\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-map-open-addressing-hash-table\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-map-open-addressing-hash-table\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_map (Open-Addressing Hash Table)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_map</code> module implements a high-performance open-addressing hash table using linear probing, power-of-two bitmask indexing, and tombstone recycling.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">Arena</span> *arena = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span> * <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-type\">HashMap</span> *map = <span class=\"tok-func\">MapCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">32</span>, arena);\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">MapSet</span>(map, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;port&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)<span class=\"tok-number\">8080</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">MapSet</span>(map, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;host&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;localhost&quot;</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> port = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">MapGet</span>(map, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;port&quot;</span>);\nassert(<span class=\"tok-func\">MapContains</span>(map, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;host&quot;</span>));\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaDestroy</span>(arena); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Bulk frees the map and all entries</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"hashmap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_map_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"and\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"mapentry\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_map_entry_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layout-hashmap-cp-map-t-and-mapentry-cp-map-entry-t\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layout-hashmap-cp-map-t-and-mapentry-cp-map-entry-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layout: <code>HashMap</code> (<code>cp_map_t</code>) and <code>MapEntry</code> (<code>cp_map_entry_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *key;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *value;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> hash;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> deleted;\n} <span class=\"tok-func\">MapEntry</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_map {\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">MapEntry</span> *entries;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> capacity;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> count;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arena_t</span> *arena;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">HashMap</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>L1 Cache Friendly Linear Probing</strong>: All slots reside in a single contiguous array of <code>MapEntry</code> structures. Probing consecutive cachelines minimizes DRAM stalls compared to separate chaining with linked lists.</li>\n<li><strong>Power-of-Two Masking</strong>: The initial capacity is clamped to the next power of two. Slot indexing uses bitwise AND (<code>hash &amp; (capacity - 1)</code>) instead of integer division (<code>hash % capacity</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Tombstone Recycling</strong>: When an element is removed via <code>MapRemove</code>, the slot is marked <code>deleted = true</code>. Subsequent insertions reuse tombstone slots, preventing artificial table bloat.</li>\n<li><strong>Dynamic Re-hashing</strong>: When load factor exceeds 70% (<code>count * 100 / capacity &gt;= 70</code>), the table doubles its capacity and re-inserts all active entries.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Guarantee</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Lookup Latency</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ average, $O(N)$ worst-case</td>\n<td>Bounded by linear probe chain</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Insertion Latency</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ amortized</td>\n<td>Triggers rehash at &gt;70% load factor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Deletion Latency</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$</td>\n<td>Marks tombstone slot</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Layout</strong></td>\n<td>Contiguous table</td>\n<td>Single allocation on Arena or Heap</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Safe for concurrent reads</td>\n<td>Requires <code>ScopedLock</code> for concurrent writes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Create Map</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapcreate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapCreate(init_cap, arena)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"create\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.create(init_cap, arena)</code></td>\n<td>Instantiate new hash map</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Set Key-Value</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapSet(map, key, val)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"set\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.set(map, key, val)</code></td>\n<td>Insert or update key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Value</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapget\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapGet(map, key)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"get\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.get(map, key)</code></td>\n<td>Retrieve void* value (NULL if missing)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Remove Key</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapremove\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapRemove(map, key)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"remove\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.remove(map, key)</code></td>\n<td>Delete key and set tombstone</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Contains Key</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapcontains\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapContains(map, key)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"contains\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.contains(map, key)</code></td>\n<td>Check existence (returns bool)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Clear Map</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapclear\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapClear(map)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"clear\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.clear(map)</code></td>\n<td>Reset count to 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Entry Count</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapcount\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapCount(map)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"count\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.count(map)</code></td>\n<td>Number of active key-value pairs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Table Capacity</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapcap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapCap(map)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"cap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.cap(map)</code></td>\n<td>Current allocated slot capacity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Destroy Map</td>\n<td><span id=\"mapdestroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>MapDestroy(map)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"destroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>map.destroy(map)</code></td>\n<td>Deallocate table memory</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>HTTP Routing Tables</strong>: Route incoming URL path strings to handler function pointers.</li>\n<li><strong>Symbol Tables &amp; AST Environments</strong>: Map variable identifiers to type/value descriptors during compilation.</li>\n<li><strong>Session &amp; Cache Registries</strong>: Track active network connections by socket descriptor string.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"configuration\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"registry\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-configuration-registry\"><a href=\"#example-configuration-registry\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: Configuration Registry</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> load_and_query_config(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span> scratch = <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchBegin</span>();\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">HashMap</span> *cfg = <span class=\"tok-func\">MapCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>, scratch.arena);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">MapSet</span>(cfg, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;db_host&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;127.0.0.1&quot;</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">MapSet</span>(cfg, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;db_port&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-number\">5432</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">MapSet</span>(cfg, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;max_connections&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-number\">100</span>);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (<span class=\"tok-func\">MapContains</span>(cfg, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;db_host&quot;</span>)) {\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *host = (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *)<span class=\"tok-func\">MapGet</span>(cfg, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;db_host&quot;</span>);\n        <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> port = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">MapGet</span>(cfg, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;db_port&quot;</span>);\n        printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Connecting to PostgreSQL at %s:%d\\n&quot;</span>, host, port);\n    }\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchEnd</span>(scratch); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Automatically frees the entire hash map</span>\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Key Lifetime</strong>: <code>MapSet</code> does not duplicate the <code>const char *key</code> string when using heap allocation. Ensure the key string remains valid for the lifetime of the map, or use <code>Arena</code> to allocate both keys and the map together.</li>\n<li><strong>NULL Value Sentinel</strong>: <code>MapGet</code> returns <code>NULL</code> when a key does not exist. Do not store raw <code>NULL</code> as a valid value if you need to differentiate missing keys from null values; use <code>MapContains</code> instead.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_args": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_args\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"command\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"line\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"argument\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"parser\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"subsystem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-args-command-line-argument-parser-subsystem\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-args-command-line-argument-parser-subsystem\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_args (Command-Line Argument Parser Subsystem)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_args</code> subsystem provides a lightweight, zero-allocation command-line argument parser supporting POSIX short flags (<code>-v</code>), long options (<code>--port 8080</code> or <code>--port=8080</code>), and positional arguments without dynamic memory overhead.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> main(<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> argc, <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> **argv) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_args_t</span> cli = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArgsParse</span>(argc, argv);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> verbose = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArgsHasFlag</span>(&amp;cli, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;-v&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--verbose&quot;</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">i64</span> port = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArgsGetInt</span>(&amp;cli, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;-p&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--port&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">8080</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *config = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArgsGetStr</span>(&amp;cli, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;-c&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--config&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;default.json&quot;</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (<span class=\"tok-func\">ArgsPositionalCount</span>(&amp;cli) &gt; <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>) {\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *input_file = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArgsGetPositional</span>(&amp;cli, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n        printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Processing input: %s\\n&quot;</span>, input_file);\n    }\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layout\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layout\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layout</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> CP_ARGS_MAX_POSITIONALS 64\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> CP_ARGS_MAX_OPTIONS     64\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> CP_ARGS_MAX_FLAGS       64\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *key;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *value;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arg_kv_t</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> argc;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> **argv;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *program_name;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *positionals[<span class=\"tok-func\">CP_ARGS_MAX_POSITIONALS</span>];\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> positional_count;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arg_kv_t</span> options[<span class=\"tok-func\">CP_ARGS_MAX_OPTIONS</span>];\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> option_count;\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *flags[<span class=\"tok-func\">CP_ARGS_MAX_FLAGS</span>];\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> flag_count;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_args_t</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<span id=\"parsing\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"semantics\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-parsing-semantics\"><a href=\"#2-2-parsing-semantics\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Parsing Semantics</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Zero Allocations</strong>: All string pointers in <code>cp_args_t</code> directly reference tokens in <code>argv</code> or string literals. No memory is allocated on the heap.</li>\n<li><strong>Short &amp; Long Syntax</strong>:</li>\n<li>Flags: Matches boolean switches like <code>-v</code>, <code>--verbose</code>, <code>-h</code>, <code>--help</code>.</li>\n<li>Key-Value Pairs: Supports both separate arguments (<code>--host 127.0.0.1</code>, <code>-p 8080</code>) and inline equals syntax (<code>--host=127.0.0.1</code>, <code>-p=8080</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Positional Isolation</strong>: Tokens not starting with <code>-</code> (or appearing after a double dash <code>--</code>) are collected sequentially into the <code>positionals</code> table.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th><code>ArgsParse</code></th>\n<th>Flag Check</th>\n<th>Option Lookup</th>\n<th>Positional Lookup</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Time Complexity</strong></td>\n<td>$O(N)$ arguments</td>\n<td>$O(F)$ flag count</td>\n<td>$O(O)$ option count</td>\n<td>$O(1)$ direct array index</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Heap Allocations</strong></td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Footprint</strong></td>\n<td>Fixed stack struct (~2 KB)</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Reentrant</td>\n<td>Read-only thread-safe</td>\n<td>Read-only thread-safe</td>\n<td>Read-only thread-safe</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Parse Arguments</td>\n<td><span id=\"argsparse\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArgsParse(argc, argv)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"parse\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>args.parse(argc, argv)</code></td>\n<td>Parse <code>argc</code>/<code>argv</code> into a populated <code>cp_args_t</code> struct</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Check Flag</td>\n<td><span id=\"argshasflag\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArgsHasFlag(a, sf, lf)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"hasflag\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>args.hasFlag(a, sf, lf)</code></td>\n<td>Check if short or long boolean flag is present</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get String Option</td>\n<td><span id=\"argsgetstr\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArgsGetStr(a, sf, lf, def)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"getstr\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>args.getStr(a, sf, lf, def)</code></td>\n<td>Extract string value by short/long switch with fallback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Integer Option</td>\n<td><span id=\"argsgetint\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArgsGetInt(a, sf, lf, def)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"getint\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>args.getInt(a, sf, lf, def)</code></td>\n<td>Extract integer value by short/long switch with fallback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Float Option</td>\n<td><span id=\"argsgetfloat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArgsGetFloat(a, sf, lf, def)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"getfloat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>args.getFloat(a, sf, lf, def)</code></td>\n<td>Extract floating-point value by short/long switch with fallback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Positional</td>\n<td><span id=\"argsgetpositional\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArgsGetPositional(a, idx)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"getpositional\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>args.getPositional(a, idx)</code></td>\n<td>Retrieve positional argument at 0-based index</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Positional Count</td>\n<td><span id=\"argspositionalcount\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ArgsPositionalCount(a)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"positionalcount\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>args.positionalCount(a)</code></td>\n<td>Total number of non-option arguments parsed</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Server CLI Flags</strong>: Configure listening port (<code>-p 8080</code>), bind address (<code>-b 0.0.0.0</code>), and daemon mode (<code>-d</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Build Tools &amp; Compilers</strong>: Parse input source files positionally alongside include paths (<code>-I include</code>) and optimization levels (<code>-O3</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Data Migrators</strong>: Accept dry-run switches (<code>--dry-run</code>), batch sizes (<code>--batch-size 1000</code>), and target database URLs.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"compilable\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-compilable-example\"><a href=\"#6-complete-compilable-example\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete Compilable Example</h2>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;assert.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> main(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Simulated CLI invocation: app --port 9090 -v --timeout=3.5 /var/log/app.log */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *mock_argv[] = {\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;app&quot;</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--port&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;9090&quot;</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;-v&quot;</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--timeout=3.5&quot;</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;/var/log/app.log&quot;</span>,\n        <span class=\"tok-type\">NULL</span>\n    };\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> mock_argc = <span class=\"tok-number\">5</span>;\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_args_t</span> parsed = args.parse(mock_argc, mock_argv);\n\n    assert(args.hasFlag(&amp;parsed, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;-v&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--verbose&quot;</span>) == <span class=\"tok-type\">true</span>);\n    assert(args.hasFlag(&amp;parsed, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;-d&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--debug&quot;</span>) == <span class=\"tok-type\">false</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">i64</span> port = args.getInt(&amp;parsed, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;-p&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--port&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">8080</span>);\n    assert(port == <span class=\"tok-number\">9090</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">f64</span> timeout = args.getFloat(&amp;parsed, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;-t&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;--timeout&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    assert(timeout &gt; <span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">49</span> &amp;&amp; timeout &lt; <span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">51</span>);\n\n    assert(args.positionalCount(&amp;parsed) == <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *target = args.getPositional(&amp;parsed, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    assert(strcmp(target, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;/var/log/app.log&quot;</span>) == <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;CLI Configuration Verified: Port=%lld, Timeout=%.1f, Positional=&#x27;%s&#x27;\\n&quot;</span>,\n           port, timeout, target);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"edge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Edge Cases</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fixed Capacity Limits</strong>: Supports up to 64 positionals, 64 options, and 64 flags. In CLI tools with hundreds of flags, increase <code>#define CP_ARGS_MAX_*</code> constants before including the header.</li>\n<li><strong>Combined Short Flags</strong>: Clustered short flags (e.g. <code>-xzvf</code>) are treated as individual single token keys rather than separated into four individual flags. Separate them into <code>-x -z -v -f</code> or check the full clustered string.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_time": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_time\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"time\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"stopwatch\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"profiling\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"subsystem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-time-time-stopwatch-amp-profiling-subsystem\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-time-time-stopwatch-amp-profiling-subsystem\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_time (Time, Stopwatch &amp; Profiling Subsystem)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_time</code> subsystem delivers nanosecond-precision monotonic timing, wall-clock ISO 8601 timestamps, explicit stopwatch measurements, and RAII-based block profiling without external library dependencies.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Nanosecond Monotonic Timestamp */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> t0 = <span class=\"tok-func\">TimeNowNs</span>();\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. RAII Auto-Cleaning Block Profiler */</span>\n{\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">ProfileScope</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Matrix Multiplication&quot;</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">// Code executes here; elapsed time is printed automatically on scope exit</span>\n}\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. Explicit Stopwatch */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">cp_stopwatch_t</span> sw = <span class=\"tok-func\">StopwatchStart</span>();\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">// ... work ...</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">StopwatchStop</span>(&amp;sw);\nprintf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Elapsed: %.2f ms\\n&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-func\">StopwatchElapsedMs</span>(&amp;sw));\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 4. ISO 8601 String */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> ts[<span class=\"tok-number\">32</span>];\n<span class=\"tok-func\">TimeIso8601</span>(ts, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(ts));\nprintf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;UTC Timestamp: %s\\n&quot;</span>, ts);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"monotonic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"clock\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"engine\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-monotonic-clock-engine\"><a href=\"#2-1-monotonic-clock-engine\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Monotonic Clock Engine</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>On POSIX platforms, <code>TimeNowNs</code> calls <code>clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &amp;ts)</code>.</li>\n<li>It converts seconds and nanoseconds into a continuous unsigned 64-bit nanosecond integer: <code>(u64)ts.tv_sec * 1000000000ULL + (u64)ts.tv_nsec</code>.</li>\n<li>Guaranteed to never step backward, even if the system wall-clock adjusts due to NTP synchronization or daylight saving shifts.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_stopwatch_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-struct-layout-cp-stopwatch-t\"><a href=\"#2-2-struct-layout-cp-stopwatch-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Struct Layout: <code>cp_stopwatch_t</code></h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> start_ns;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> stop_ns;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> running;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_stopwatch_t</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Can be started, stopped, reset, or queried across various units (nanoseconds, microseconds, milliseconds, seconds).</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"raii\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"profiler\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"profilescope\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-3-raii-profiler-profilescope\"><a href=\"#2-3-raii-profiler-profilescope\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.3 RAII Profiler: <code>ProfileScope</code></h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *name;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> start_ns;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">_cp_prof_scope_t</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#define</span> ProfileScope(name_str) \\\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">_cp_prof_scope_t</span> <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_CONCAT</span>(_prof_scope_, __LINE__) __attribute__((cleanup(_cp_prof_scope_cleanup), unused)) = \\\n        { .name = (name_str), .start_ns = cp_time_now_ns() }</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Uses GCC/Clang <code>__attribute__((cleanup))</code> to invoke <code>_cp_prof_scope_cleanup</code> automatically when leaving the lexical block.</li>\n<li>Zero runtime overhead when not executing; 0 heap allocations.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Precision</th>\n<th>Clock Source</th>\n<th>Monotonic</th>\n<th>Heap Allocations</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"timenowns\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeNowNs</code></td>\n<td>1 ns</td>\n<td><span id=\"clock_monotonic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>CLOCK_MONOTONIC</code></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"timenowus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeNowUs</code></td>\n<td>1 us</td>\n<td><span id=\"clock_monotonic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>CLOCK_MONOTONIC</code></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"timenowms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeNowMs</code></td>\n<td>1 ms</td>\n<td><span id=\"clock_monotonic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>CLOCK_MONOTONIC</code></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"timeunixsec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeUnixSec</code></td>\n<td>1 s</td>\n<td><span id=\"clock_realtime\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>CLOCK_REALTIME</code></td>\n<td>No (Wall clock)</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"timeiso8601\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeIso8601</code></td>\n<td>1 s</td>\n<td><code>gmtime_r</code> / <code>gmtime</code></td>\n<td>No (Wall clock)</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"profilescope\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ProfileScope</code></td>\n<td>1 ns</td>\n<td><span id=\"clock_monotonic\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>CLOCK_MONOTONIC</code></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Now (Nanoseconds)</td>\n<td><span id=\"timenowns\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeNowNs()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"nowns\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>time_api.nowNs()</code></td>\n<td>Current monotonic timestamp in nanoseconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Now (Microseconds)</td>\n<td><span id=\"timenowus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeNowUs()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"nowus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>time_api.nowUs()</code></td>\n<td>Current monotonic timestamp in fractional microseconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Now (Milliseconds)</td>\n<td><span id=\"timenowms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeNowMs()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"nowms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>time_api.nowMs()</code></td>\n<td>Current monotonic timestamp in fractional milliseconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unix Epoch Seconds</td>\n<td><span id=\"timeunixsec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeUnixSec()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"unixsec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>time_api.unixSec()</code></td>\n<td>Standard UTC timestamp in seconds since 1970</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sleep (ms)</td>\n<td><span id=\"timesleepms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeSleepMs(ms)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sleepms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>time_api.sleepMs(ms)</code></td>\n<td>Suspend thread execution for specified milliseconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sleep (us)</td>\n<td><span id=\"timesleepus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeSleepUs(us)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sleepus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>time_api.sleepUs(us)</code></td>\n<td>Suspend thread execution for specified microseconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ISO 8601 Stamp</td>\n<td><span id=\"timeiso8601\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>TimeIso8601(buf, cap)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"iso8601\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>time_api.iso8601(buf, cap)</code></td>\n<td>Format UTC timestamp as <code>YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Start Stopwatch</td>\n<td><span id=\"stopwatchstart\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StopwatchStart()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"start\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stopwatch.start()</code></td>\n<td>Instantiate and activate a new stopwatch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stop Stopwatch</td>\n<td><span id=\"stopwatchstop\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StopwatchStop(sw)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"stop\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stopwatch.stop(sw)</code></td>\n<td>Pause active stopwatch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Reset Stopwatch</td>\n<td><span id=\"stopwatchreset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StopwatchReset(sw)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"reset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stopwatch.reset(sw)</code></td>\n<td>Reset stopwatch counters to zero</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Elapsed Ns</td>\n<td><span id=\"stopwatchelapsedns\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StopwatchElapsedNs(sw)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"elapsedns\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stopwatch.elapsedNs(sw)</code></td>\n<td>Calculate elapsed nanoseconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Elapsed Us</td>\n<td><span id=\"stopwatchelapsedus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StopwatchElapsedUs(sw)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"elapsedus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stopwatch.elapsedUs(sw)</code></td>\n<td>Calculate elapsed microseconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Elapsed Ms</td>\n<td><span id=\"stopwatchelapsedms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StopwatchElapsedMs(sw)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"elapsedms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stopwatch.elapsedMs(sw)</code></td>\n<td>Calculate elapsed milliseconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Elapsed Sec</td>\n<td><span id=\"stopwatchelapsedsec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StopwatchElapsedSec(sw)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"elapsedsec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stopwatch.elapsedSec(sw)</code></td>\n<td>Calculate elapsed seconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Profile Scope</td>\n<td><span id=\"profilescope\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>ProfileScope(name)</code></td>\n<td>-</td>\n<td>RAII block benchmark logger</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Low-Latency Benchmarking</strong>: Measure subroutine latency down to single-digit nanoseconds without profiler skew.</li>\n<li><strong>Deterministic Frame Pacing</strong>: Maintain fixed 60 FPS / 144 FPS game loop ticks by computing <code>delta_time = TimeNowNs() - last_frame_ns</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Structured Event Logs</strong>: Prefix telemetry and network packets with standardized ISO 8601 strings.</li>\n<li><strong>Scope Profiling</strong>: Rapidly identify algorithmic bottlenecks across nested blocks using <code>ProfileScope</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"compilable\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-compilable-example\"><a href=\"#6-complete-compilable-example\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete Compilable Example</h2>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;assert.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> main(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Monotonic timing */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> t1 = time_api.nowNs();\n    time_api.sleepMs(<span class=\"tok-number\">5</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> t2 = time_api.nowNs();\n    assert(t2 &gt; t1);\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Sleep interval: %llu ns\\n&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"tok-type\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">long</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">long</span>)(t2 - t1));\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Stopwatch */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_stopwatch_t</span> sw = stopwatch.start();\n    time_api.sleepMs(<span class=\"tok-number\">10</span>);\n    stopwatch.stop(&amp;sw);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">f64</span> ms = stopwatch.elapsedMs(&amp;sw);\n    assert(ms &gt;= <span class=\"tok-number\">9</span>.<span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Stopwatch measured: %.2f ms\\n&quot;</span>, ms);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. ISO 8601 Formatting */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> buf[<span class=\"tok-number\">32</span>];\n    time_api.iso8601(buf, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(buf));\n    assert(strlen(buf) == <span class=\"tok-number\">20</span>); <span class=\"tok-comment\">// &quot;YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ&quot;</span>\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Current ISO timestamp: %s\\n&quot;</span>, buf);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 4. RAII Scoped profiler */</span>\n    {\n        <span class=\"tok-func\">ProfileScope</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Transient Compute Block&quot;</span>);\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">volatile</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> sum = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>; i &lt; <span class=\"tok-number\">100000</span>; i++) {\n            sum += i;\n        }\n    }\n\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"edge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Edge Cases</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Resolution Dependent on Kernel</strong>: While <code>TimeNowNs</code> returns integer nanoseconds, hardware timers and OS kernel ticks dictate the ultimate precision (typically 1 to 10 ns on modern x86-64 hardware).</li>\n<li><strong>Sleep Granularity</strong>: <code>TimeSleepMs</code> and <code>TimeSleepUs</code> call the OS scheduler. Actual sleep duration may be extended by scheduler scheduling quanta (~0.1 ms to 1 ms).</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_json": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_json\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"micro\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"json\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"parser\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"subsystem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-json-micro-json-parser-subsystem\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-json-micro-json-parser-subsystem\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_json (Micro JSON Parser Subsystem)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_json</code> subsystem is an in-situ, zero-allocation micro JSON parser compliant with RFC 8259. It navigates JSON payloads by returning <code>StrView</code> non-owning string slices without performing heap allocations or mutating the input buffer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *payload = <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;{\\&quot;</span>status\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;:200,\\&quot;</span>success\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;:true,\\&quot;</span>nodes\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;:[\\&quot;</span>srv-<span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;,\\&quot;</span>srv-<span class=\"tok-number\">2</span>\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;]}&quot;</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-type\">cp_json_val_t</span> root = <span class=\"tok-func\">JsonParse</span>(payload, strlen(payload));\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">i64</span> status = <span class=\"tok-func\">JsonAsInt</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">JsonGet</span>(root, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;status&quot;</span>), <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);           <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 200</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> ok = <span class=\"tok-func\">JsonAsBool</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">JsonGet</span>(root, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;success&quot;</span>), <span class=\"tok-type\">false</span>);        <span class=\"tok-comment\">// true</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">cp_json_val_t</span> nodes = <span class=\"tok-func\">JsonGet</span>(root, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;nodes&quot;</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> count = <span class=\"tok-func\">JsonLen</span>(nodes);                                 <span class=\"tok-comment\">// 2</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> first_node = <span class=\"tok-func\">JsonAsView</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">JsonAt</span>(nodes, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>));            <span class=\"tok-comment\">// &quot;srv-1&quot;</span></code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"types\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"and\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"data\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"structures\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-types-and-data-structures\"><a href=\"#2-1-types-and-data-structures\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Types and Data Structures</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">enum</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_INVALID</span> = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>,\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_NULL</span>,\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_BOOL</span>,\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_NUMBER</span>,\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_STRING</span>,\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_ARRAY</span>,\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_OBJECT</span>\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_json_type_t</span>;\n\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> raw;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_json_type_t</span> type;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_json_val_t</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<span id=\"memory\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"model\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"traversal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-memory-model-amp-traversal\"><a href=\"#2-2-memory-model-amp-traversal\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Memory Model &amp; Traversal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Zero Allocations</strong>: <code>cp_json_val_t</code> references a slice of the original buffer via <code>StrView</code> (<code>const char *data</code>, <code>usize len</code>). No memory is allocated on the heap or arena during parsing.</li>\n<li><strong>In-Situ Tokenization</strong>: <code>cp_json_parse</code> validates syntactic boundaries (braces, brackets, quotes, numbers) and detects root element types in a single linear pass.</li>\n<li><strong>Key &amp; Index Traversal</strong>:</li>\n<li><code>JsonGet(obj, key)</code> scans keys within JSON object <code>{ ... }</code>, skipping nested container levels by tracking structural balance counters <code>{}</code>, <code>[]</code>, and quotes.</li>\n<li><code>JsonAt(arr, index)</code> steps through array elements <code>[ ... ]</code> using structural delimiter commas <code>,</code> until the target index is reached.</li>\n<li><strong>Conversion Primitives</strong>:</li>\n<li><code>JsonAsView</code>: Strips enclosing quote delimiters for strings or returns raw numeric/literal slices.</li>\n<li><code>JsonAsInt</code> / <code>JsonAsFloat</code>: Parses integer or floating point values directly from the underlying byte slice.</li>\n<li><code>JsonAsBool</code>: Checks slice against literal <code>\"true\"</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>Time Complexity</th>\n<th>Auxiliary Memory</th>\n<th>Heap Allocations</th>\n<th>Input Mutation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"jsonparse\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonParse</code></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ root detection</td>\n<td>0 bytes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>None (read-only)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"jsonget\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonGet</code></td>\n<td>$O(N)$ key scan</td>\n<td>0 bytes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>None (read-only)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"jsonat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonAt</code></td>\n<td>$O(K)$ index scan</td>\n<td>0 bytes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>None (read-only)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span id=\"jsonlen\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonLen</code></td>\n<td>$O(N)$ container scan</td>\n<td>0 bytes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>None (read-only)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>JsonAsInt</code> / <code>Float</code></td>\n<td>$O(D)$ digit count</td>\n<td>0 bytes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>None (read-only)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Parse JSON</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonparse\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonParse(str, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"parse\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.parse(str, len)</code></td>\n<td>Parse JSON buffer into root <code>cp_json_val_t</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Key Value</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonget\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonGet(obj, key)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"get\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.get(obj, key)</code></td>\n<td>Query member of JSON object by key name</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Array Item</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonAt(arr, index)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"at\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.at(arr, index)</code></td>\n<td>Retrieve element at 0-based index from array</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Container Length</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonlen\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonLen(val)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"len\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.len(val)</code></td>\n<td>Count elements in JSON object or array</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unquote View</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonasview\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonAsView(val)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"asview\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.asView(val)</code></td>\n<td>Return unquoted <code>StrView</code> string slice</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read Integer</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonasint\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonAsInt(val, def)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"asint\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.asInt(val, def)</code></td>\n<td>Convert numeric node to <code>i64</code> with fallback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read Float</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonasfloat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonAsFloat(val, def)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"asfloat\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.asFloat(val, def)</code></td>\n<td>Convert numeric node to <code>f64</code> with fallback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read Boolean</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonasbool\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonAsBool(val, def)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"asbool\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.asBool(val, def)</code></td>\n<td>Convert boolean node to <code>bool</code> with fallback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Check Null</td>\n<td><span id=\"jsonisnull\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>JsonIsNull(val)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"isnull\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>json_api.isNull(val)</code></td>\n<td>Check if node represents JSON <code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>REST API Response Inspection</strong>: Extract configuration parameters, bearer tokens, or error status codes directly from HTTP response payloads.</li>\n<li><strong>Embedded Config Files</strong>: Read application configuration schemas in JSON format without dragging in bloated multi-megabyte C++ parsing libraries.</li>\n<li><strong>Telemetry &amp; Log Querying</strong>: Fast-path inspection of structured JSON log records over high-bandwidth TCP streams.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"compilable\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-compilable-example\"><a href=\"#6-complete-compilable-example\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete Compilable Example</h2>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;assert.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> main(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *payload = \n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;{\\n&quot;</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;  \\&quot;</span>host\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;: \\&quot;</span>api.internal.net\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;,\\n&quot;</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;  \\&quot;</span>port\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;: 8443,\\n&quot;</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;  \\&quot;</span>tls\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;: true,\\n&quot;</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;  \\&quot;</span>replicas\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;: [\\&quot;</span>node-a\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;, \\&quot;</span>node-b\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;, \\&quot;</span>node-c\\<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;]\\n&quot;</span>\n        <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;}&quot;</span>;\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_json_val_t</span> root = json_api.parse(payload, strlen(payload));\n    assert(root.type == <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_OBJECT</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Query object fields */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_json_val_t</span> host_val = json_api.get(root, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;host&quot;</span>);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> host_sv = json_api.asView(host_val);\n    assert(<span class=\"tok-func\">StrViewEqStr</span>(host_sv, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;api.internal.net&quot;</span>));\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">i64</span> port = json_api.asInt(json_api.get(root, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;port&quot;</span>), <span class=\"tok-number\">80</span>);\n    assert(port == <span class=\"tok-number\">8443</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> tls = json_api.asBool(json_api.get(root, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;tls&quot;</span>), <span class=\"tok-type\">false</span>);\n    assert(tls == <span class=\"tok-type\">true</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* Query array */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_json_val_t</span> replicas = json_api.get(root, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;replicas&quot;</span>);\n    assert(replicas.type == <span class=\"tok-func\">CP_JSON_ARRAY</span>);\n    assert(json_api.len(replicas) == <span class=\"tok-number\">3</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> first_replica = json_api.asView(json_api.at(replicas, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>));\n    assert(<span class=\"tok-func\">StrViewEqStr</span>(first_replica, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;node-a&quot;</span>));\n\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Parsed configuration for %.*s on port %lld (TLS: %d)\\n&quot;</span>,\n           (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)host_sv.len, host_sv.data, port, tls);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"edge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Edge Cases</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Non-Materializing Parser</strong>: <code>cp_json</code> is an inspector and query engine, not a serializer or mutating DOM tree.</li>\n<li><strong>Escape Sequences</strong>: <code>JsonAsView</code> returns raw byte slices referencing the input buffer. Escape sequences such as <code>\\n</code> or <code>\\uXXXX</code> remain unescaped. If escaped characters require unescaping, copy them into an <code>Arena</code> or <code>String</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Large Container Scan Latency</strong>: Because <code>cp_json</code> does not construct an auxiliary index, <code>JsonAt</code> on an array of 100,000 items scans sequentially from element 0. For repeated queries over huge arrays, parse elements into a <code>Vec(T)</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_stack": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_stack\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cache\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"lifo\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"stack\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-stack-l1-cache-lifo-stack\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-stack-l1-cache-lifo-stack\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_stack (L1 Cache LIFO Stack)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_stack</code> module implements a cacheline-aligned LIFO stack optimized for sub-nanosecond push and pop operations, featuring top-relative indexed peeking (<code>StackGet</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">Arena</span> *arena = <span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">64</span> * <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-type\">Stack</span> *s = <span class=\"tok-func\">StackCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>, arena);\n\n<span class=\"tok-func\">StackPush</span>(s, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)<span class=\"tok-number\">10</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">StackPush</span>(s, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)<span class=\"tok-number\">20</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">// Index 0 is the top (20), index 1 is next down (10)</span>\nassert((<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">StackGet</span>(s, <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>) == <span class=\"tok-number\">20</span>);\nassert((<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">StackGet</span>(s, <span class=\"tok-number\">1</span>) == <span class=\"tok-number\">10</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> top = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">StackPop</span>(s);\n<span class=\"tok-func\">ArenaDestroy</span>(arena);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"struct\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"layout\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"stack\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_stack_t\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-struct-layout-stack-cp-stack-t\"><a href=\"#2-1-struct-layout-stack-cp-stack-t\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Struct Layout: <code>Stack</code> (<code>cp_stack_t</code>)</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">struct</span> cp_stack {\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> **data;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> top;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> capacity;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">cp_arena_t</span> *arena;\n} <span class=\"tok-type\">Stack</span>;</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Top-Relative Indexing</strong>: <code>StackGet(s, index_from_top)</code> evaluates to <code>s-&gt;data[s-&gt;top - 1 - index_from_top]</code>. This eliminates tedious manual arithmetic when inspecting operands in virtual machines, AST evaluators, and recursive descent parsers.</li>\n<li><strong>Dual Memory Backing</strong>: When <code>arena</code> is provided, the buffer grows linearly inside the arena. When <code>arena</code> is <code>NULL</code>, standard <code>malloc</code>/<code>realloc</code>/<code>free</code> is used.</li>\n<li><strong>Fast-Path Inlining</strong>: <code>StackPush</code> and <code>StackPop</code> are implemented as inlined macros checking bounds before executing single-pointer loads/stores.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Guarantee</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Push Latency</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$ amortized</td>\n<td>Doubles capacity when <code>top == capacity</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pop Latency</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$</td>\n<td>Single decrement and read</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Peek / Indexed Get</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$</td>\n<td>Direct array access relative to top</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Heap Allocations</strong></td>\n<td>0 when Arena-backed</td>\n<td>1 array buffer when heap-backed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread-Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Thread-confined</td>\n<td>Requires <code>ScopedLock(&amp;mutex)</code> if shared</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Create Stack</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackcreate\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackCreate(cap, arena)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"create\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.create(cap, arena)</code></td>\n<td>Instantiate stack with initial capacity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Push Item</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackpush\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackPush(s, item)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"push\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.push(s, item)</code></td>\n<td>Push void* item onto top</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pop Item</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackpop\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackPop(s)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"pop\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.pop(s)</code></td>\n<td>Remove and return top void* (NULL if empty)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Peek Top</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackpeek\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackPeek(s)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"peek\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.peek(s)</code></td>\n<td>Read top item without popping</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Indexed Get</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackget\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackGet(s, idx_from_top)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"get\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.get(s, idx_from_top)</code></td>\n<td>Read item relative to top (0 = top)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stack Length</td>\n<td><span id=\"stacklen\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackLen(s)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"len\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.len(s)</code></td>\n<td>Current number of items on stack</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stack Capacity</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackcap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackCap(s)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"cap\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.cap(s)</code></td>\n<td>Current allocated capacity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Is Empty</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackisempty\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackIsEmpty(s)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"isempty\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.isEmpty(s)</code></td>\n<td>Returns true if stack length is 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Clear Stack</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackclear\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackClear(s)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"clear\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.clear(s)</code></td>\n<td>Reset top index to 0 without freeing memory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Destroy Stack</td>\n<td><span id=\"stackdestroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>StackDestroy(s)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"destroy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>stack.destroy(s)</code></td>\n<td>Deallocate stack and buffer</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Reverse Polish Notation (RPN) Calculators</strong>: Push numbers as operands; pop and evaluate on operators.</li>\n<li><strong>Backtracking and Depth-First Traversal</strong>: Track visited paths without recursion stack overflow.</li>\n<li><strong>Bytecode Interpreters</strong>: Fast operand stack for execution engines.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"c11\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"usage\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"examples\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-c11-usage-examples\"><a href=\"#6-complete-c11-usage-examples\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete C11 Usage Examples</h2>\n<span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"expression\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"evaluation\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"example-expression-evaluation\"><a href=\"#example-expression-evaluation\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Example: Expression Evaluation</h3>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> evaluate_rpn(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *expr) {\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">TempArena</span> scratch = <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchBegin</span>();\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">Stack</span> *s = <span class=\"tok-func\">StackCreate</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">16</span>, scratch.arena);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> count = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> *tokens = <span class=\"tok-func\">StrSplitArena</span>(<span class=\"tok-func\">StrFromC</span>(expr), <span class=\"tok-string\">&#x27; &#x27;</span>, scratch.arena, &amp;count);\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> i = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>; i &lt; count; i++) {\n        <span class=\"tok-func\">StrView</span> t = tokens[i];\n        <span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (<span class=\"tok-func\">StrEqualsC</span>(t, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;+&quot;</span>)) {\n            <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> b = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">StackPop</span>(s);\n            <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> a = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">StackPop</span>(s);\n            <span class=\"tok-func\">StackPush</span>(s, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)(a + b));\n        } <span class=\"tok-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"tok-keyword\">if</span> (<span class=\"tok-func\">StrEqualsC</span>(t, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;*&quot;</span>)) {\n            <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> b = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">StackPop</span>(s);\n            <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> a = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">StackPop</span>(s);\n            <span class=\"tok-func\">StackPush</span>(s, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)(a * b));\n        } <span class=\"tok-keyword\">else</span> {\n            <span class=\"tok-func\">StackPush</span>(s, (<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span> *)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)atoi(t.data));\n        }\n    }\n    \n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> result = (<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span>)(<span class=\"tok-type\">intptr_t</span>)<span class=\"tok-func\">StackPop</span>(s);\n    <span class=\"tok-func\">ScratchEnd</span>(scratch);\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> result;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"constraints\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-operational-constraints\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Operational Constraints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Void Pointer Casts</strong>: Stores items as <code>void*</code>. When storing primitive integers, cast via <code>(void*)(intptr_t)val</code> to maintain portability across 32-bit and 64-bit architectures.</li>\n<li><strong>Index Bounds in <code>StackGet</code></strong>: Passing <code>index_from_top &gt;= StackLen(s)</code> safely returns <code>NULL</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
  "cp_os": "<span id=\"module\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"specification\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cp_os\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"operating\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"system\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"process\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"subsystem\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h1 id=\"module-specification-cp-os-operating-system-amp-process-subsystem\"><a href=\"#module-specification-cp-os-operating-system-amp-process-subsystem\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> Module Specification: cp_os (Operating System &amp; Process Subsystem)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-tl-dr\"><a href=\"#1-tl-dr\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 1. TL;DR</h2>\n<p>The <code>cp_os</code> subsystem provides portable, low-overhead system queries, process execution, environment variable management, and sub-millisecond sleep routines without external dependencies.</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Inspect Hardware &amp; Environment */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u32</span> cores = <span class=\"tok-func\">OsNumCpus</span>();\n<span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> ram_mb = <span class=\"tok-func\">OsTotalRamBytes</span>() / (<span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span> * <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>);\n<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *user = <span class=\"tok-func\">OsEnvGetOr</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;USER&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;unknown&quot;</span>);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Execute Subprocess &amp; Capture Output */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> output[<span class=\"tok-number\">512</span>];\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> exit_code = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n<span class=\"tok-type\">i64</span> bytes = <span class=\"tok-func\">OsExec</span>(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;uname -r&quot;</span>, output, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(output), &amp;exit_code);\n\n<span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. High-Precision Sleep */</span>\n<span class=\"tok-func\">OsSleepMs</span>(<span class=\"tok-number\">10</span>);</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"formal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"definitions\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internal\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"architecture\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\"><a href=\"#2-formal-definitions-amp-internal-architecture\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2. Formal Definitions &amp; Internal Architecture</h2>\n<span id=\"process\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"execution\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"model\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-1-process-execution-model\"><a href=\"#2-1-process-execution-model\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.1 Process Execution Model</h3>\n<p><code>OsExec</code> runs child processes through synchronous pipe redirection:</p>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-type\">i64</span> cp_os_exec(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *cmd, <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> *out_buf, <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> out_cap, <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> *exit_code);</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Spawns a shell subshell via <code>popen()</code> in read mode.</li>\n<li>Streams standard output incrementally into the destination buffer <code>out_buf</code> up to <code>out_cap - 1</code> bytes.</li>\n<li>Null-terminates the resulting buffer and stores the child exit code via <code>pclose()</code>.</li>\n<li>Returns the total bytes written, or <code>-1</code> on fork/execution failure.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"hardware\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"query\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"internals\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-2-hardware-query-internals\"><a href=\"#2-2-hardware-query-internals\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.2 Hardware Query Internals</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>CPU Cores (<code>OsNumCpus</code>)</strong>: Evaluates <code>sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN)</code> on POSIX systems or <code>GetSystemInfo</code> on Windows.</li>\n<li><strong>Physical RAM (<code>OsTotalRamBytes</code>, <code>OsAvailRamBytes</code>)</strong>: Evaluates <code>sysconf(_SC_PHYS_PAGES) * sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE)</code> on Linux/POSIX or <code>GlobalMemoryStatusEx</code> on Windows.</li>\n<li><strong>Page Size (<code>OsPageSize</code>)</strong>: Queries system virtual memory page boundary (typically 4096 bytes).</li>\n<li><strong>Process Identifiers (<code>OsPid</code>, <code>OsPpid</code>)</strong>: Direct bindings to <code>getpid()</code> and <code>getppid()</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<span id=\"non\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"busy\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"sleep\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h3 id=\"2-3-non-busy-sleep\"><a href=\"#2-3-non-busy-sleep\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 2.3 Non-Busy Sleep</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>OsSleepMs(u32 ms)</code> and <code>OsSleepUs(u64 us)</code> translate directly to <code>nanosleep()</code> on POSIX platforms, yielding execution time slices back to the kernel scheduler without high CPU spin cycles.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"operational\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"guarantees\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"contracts\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\"><a href=\"#3-operational-guarantees-amp-contracts\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 3. Operational Guarantees &amp; Contracts</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Hardware Queries</th>\n<th>Subprocess Exec</th>\n<th>Env Access</th>\n<th>Non-Busy Sleep</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Time Complexity</strong></td>\n<td>$O(1)$</td>\n<td>$O(T)$ child execution time</td>\n<td>$O(K)$ hash/table lookup</td>\n<td>$O(\\Delta t)$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Heap Allocations</strong></td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>Internal libc pipe buffer</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Memory Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Buffer size bounded</td>\n<td>Null-terminated string guarantee</td>\n<td>Returns immutable slice/copy</td>\n<td>Safe</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Thread Safety</strong></td>\n<td>Thread-safe</td>\n<td>Thread-safe (POSIX <code>popen</code>)</td>\n<td>Read thread-safe, write requires synchronization</td>\n<td>Thread-safe</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"api\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"matrix\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"4-api-matrix\"><a href=\"#4-api-matrix\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 4. API Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>PascalCase Macro</th>\n<th>Dot-Notation API</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Run Subprocess</td>\n<td><span id=\"osexec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsExec(cmd, buf, cap, code)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"exec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.exec(cmd, buf, cap, code)</code></td>\n<td>Synchronous command execution with output capture</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CPU Core Count</td>\n<td><span id=\"osnumcpus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsNumCpus()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"numcpus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.numCpus()</code></td>\n<td>Count of online logical processor cores</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Total RAM</td>\n<td><span id=\"ostotalrambytes\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsTotalRamBytes()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"totalrambytes\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.totalRamBytes()</code></td>\n<td>Total physical system RAM in bytes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Available RAM</td>\n<td><span id=\"osavailrambytes\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsAvailRamBytes()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"availrambytes\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.availRamBytes()</code></td>\n<td>Free/available physical system RAM in bytes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Page Size</td>\n<td><span id=\"ospagesize\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsPageSize()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"pagesize\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.pageSize()</code></td>\n<td>Virtual memory page size in bytes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hostname</td>\n<td><span id=\"oshostname\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsHostname(buf, len)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"hostname\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.hostname(buf, len)</code></td>\n<td>System network node hostname</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Uptime</td>\n<td><span id=\"osuptimesec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsUptimeSec()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"uptimesec\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.uptimeSec()</code></td>\n<td>System uptime in seconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Process ID</td>\n<td><span id=\"ospid\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsPid()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"pid\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.pid()</code></td>\n<td>Current process identifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Parent PID</td>\n<td><span id=\"osppid\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsPpid()</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"ppid\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.ppid()</code></td>\n<td>Parent process identifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Send Signal</td>\n<td><span id=\"oskill\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsKill(pid, sig)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"kill\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.kill(pid, sig)</code></td>\n<td>Dispatch POSIX signal to target PID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Process Alive</td>\n<td><span id=\"osisrunning\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsIsRunning(pid)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"isrunning\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.isRunning(pid)</code></td>\n<td>Check if target PID exists and responds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Env</td>\n<td><span id=\"osenvget\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsEnvGet(name)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"envget\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.envGet(name)</code></td>\n<td>Fetch environment variable value or NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Env Default</td>\n<td><span id=\"osenvgetor\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsEnvGetOr(name, def)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"envgetor\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.envGetOr(name, def)</code></td>\n<td>Fetch environment variable or fallback string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get Env Int</td>\n<td><span id=\"osenvgetint\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsEnvGetInt(name, def)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"envgetint\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.envGetInt(name, def)</code></td>\n<td>Parse integer environment variable with fallback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Set Env</td>\n<td><span id=\"osenvset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsEnvSet(name, val)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"envset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.envSet(name, val)</code></td>\n<td>Modify or create environment variable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unset Env</td>\n<td><span id=\"osenvunset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsEnvUnset(name)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"envunset\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.envUnset(name)</code></td>\n<td>Remove environment variable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Has Env</td>\n<td><span id=\"osenvhas\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsEnvHas(name)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"envhas\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.envHas(name)</code></td>\n<td>Check existence of environment variable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sleep (ms)</td>\n<td><span id=\"ossleepms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsSleepMs(ms)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sleepms\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.sleepMs(ms)</code></td>\n<td>Pause execution for millisecond duration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sleep (us)</td>\n<td><span id=\"ossleepus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>OsSleepUs(us)</code></td>\n<td><span id=\"sleepus\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><code>os.sleepUs(us)</code></td>\n<td>Pause execution for microsecond duration</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"use\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"5-use-cases\"><a href=\"#5-use-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 5. Use Cases</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Dynamic Thread Pool Sizing</strong>: Automatically size thread pools at application startup based on online processor count (<code>OsNumCpus()</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>System Health Monitors</strong>: Track host memory consumption and system uptime inside daemon health checks.</li>\n<li><strong>Subprocess Management</strong>: Execute external command-line utilities, compilers, or diagnostics and parse output into caller-allocated buffers.</li>\n<li><strong>Environment-Driven Configuration</strong>: Read operational ports, log levels, or configuration tokens with fallback defaults (<code>OsEnvGetInt(\"PORT\", 8080)</code>).</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"complete\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"compilable\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"example\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"6-complete-compilable-example\"><a href=\"#6-complete-compilable-example\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 6. Complete Compilable Example</h2>\n<div class=\"code-container\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">C</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"code-pre\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;cplus/cplus.h&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"tok-macro\">#include</span> <span class=\"tok-string\">&lt;assert.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> main(<span class=\"tok-keyword\">void</span>) {\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 1. Host hardware diagnostics */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u32</span> cores = os.numCpus();\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> total_ram = os.totalRamBytes();\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">u64</span> avail_ram = os.availRamBytes();\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span> page_sz = os.pageSize();\n\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;Hardware: %u Cores | RAM: %llu MB Total / %llu MB Available | Page: %zu B\\n&quot;</span>,\n           cores,\n           (<span class=\"tok-type\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">long</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">long</span>)(total_ram / (<span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span> * <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>)),\n           (<span class=\"tok-type\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">long</span> <span class=\"tok-type\">long</span>)(avail_ram / (<span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span> * <span class=\"tok-number\">1024</span>)),\n           page_sz);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 2. Process inspection */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">i32</span> pid = os.pid();\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">i32</span> ppid = os.ppid();\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">bool</span> alive = os.isRunning(pid);\n    assert(alive == <span class=\"tok-type\">true</span>);\n    printf(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;PID: %d (Parent: %d) Alive: %d\\n&quot;</span>, pid, ppid, alive);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 3. Environment variable management */</span>\n    os.envSet(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;CPLUS_TEST_VAR&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;active&quot;</span>);\n    assert(os.envHas(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;CPLUS_TEST_VAR&quot;</span>) == <span class=\"tok-type\">true</span>);\n    assert(strcmp(os.envGet(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;CPLUS_TEST_VAR&quot;</span>), <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;active&quot;</span>) == <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">i64</span> port = os.envGetInt(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;CPLUS_PORT&quot;</span>, <span class=\"tok-number\">9000</span>);\n    assert(port == <span class=\"tok-number\">9000</span>);\n\n    os.envUnset(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;CPLUS_TEST_VAR&quot;</span>);\n    assert(os.envHas(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;CPLUS_TEST_VAR&quot;</span>) == <span class=\"tok-type\">false</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-comment\">/* 4. Subprocess execution */</span>\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">char</span> buf[<span class=\"tok-number\">256</span>];\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">int</span> code = <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n    <span class=\"tok-type\">i64</span> bytes = os.exec(<span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;echo -n &#x27;hello world&#x27;&quot;</span>, buf, <span class=\"tok-keyword\">sizeof</span>(buf), &amp;code);\n    assert(bytes &gt; <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    assert(code == <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n    assert(strcmp(buf, <span class=\"tok-string\">&quot;hello world&quot;</span>) == <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"tok-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"tok-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<hr />\n<span id=\"limitations\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"amp\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"edge\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><span id=\"cases\" class=\"anchor-target\"></span><h2 id=\"7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\"><a href=\"#7-limitations-amp-edge-cases\" class=\"heading-anchor\">#</a> 7. Limitations &amp; Edge Cases</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Command Shell Dependency</strong>: <code>OsExec</code> invokes <code>/bin/sh -c</code> on POSIX systems. Ensure untrusted inputs are sanitized to avoid shell injection vulnerabilities.</li>\n<li><strong>Process Output Buffering</strong>: If subprocess output exceeds the capacity of <code>out_buf</code>, trailing bytes are discarded. To process arbitrary streams, consume data via custom pipes or temporary files.</li>\n<li><strong>Environment Mutability</strong>: <code>OsEnvSet</code> is not thread-safe if other threads call <code>getenv()</code> concurrently without a shared lock.</li>\n</ul>"
};
